/	P?S/8 ASCII PAPER-TAPE UTILITY

/	LAST EDIT:	20-NOV-2015	05:00:00	CJL

/	MUST BE ASSEMBLED WITH THE '/J' [PAL8 '/F'] OPTION SWITCH CLEAR.

/	P?S/8 ASCII TEXT-ORIENTED PAPER-TAPE UTILITY TO CONVERT P?S/8 TEXT FILES
/	FROM/TO ASCII PAPER-TAPES AS GENERALLY USED IN THE SO-CALLED "PAPER TAPE
/	OPERATING SYSTEM" [WHICH IS ACTUALLY JUST A BUNCH OF VAGUELY RELATED
/	STAND-ALONE UTILITIES THAT CAN BE USED TO DEVELOP SHORT PDP-8 PROGRAMS AT
/	GREAT EXPENSE OF TIME AND EFFORT ON A MACHINE WITHOUT A STORAGE DEVICE].

/	PTUTIL WAS WRITTEN PRIMARILY TO ENHANCE THE SIMULATED PDP-8 ENVIRONMENT
/	IMPLEMENTED IN THE P?S ADVANCED SIMH PACKAGE [PASP], AN ADVANCED
/	CONFIGURATION OF THE SIMH PDP-8 SIMULATOR.  BY TAKING ADVANTAGE OF SPECIFIC
/	FEATURES ONLY AVAILABLE WHEN RUNNING THE SIMH SIMULATOR FROM RECENT RELEASES
/	OF MICROSOFT WINDOWS, THE OVERALL IMPLEMENTATION ALLOWS REALISTIC PDP-8
/	PROGRAM DEVELOPMENT.  HOWEVER, P?S/8 [AS CURRENTLY DISTRIBUTED] LACKS AN
/	APPROPRIATE MECHANISM TO DIRECTLY INTERFACE WITH FILES OBTAINED FROM THE HOST
/	[WINDOWS] ENVIRONMENT.

/	PRIOR TO THE CREATION OF THE PTUTIL PROGRAM, THE PROCESS REQUIRED THE USE OF
/	OS/8 TO RECEIVE THE FILE UNDER DEVELOPMENT VIA THE PTR: HANDLER WHILE ENSURING
/	THE LIMITATIONS OF THIS PROCESS DID NOT INTERFERE WITH THE OUTCOME.  [NOTE:
/	THE OS/8 HANDLER IS FLAWED; PTUTIL IMPLEMENTS SUFFICIENT FEATURES TO PREVENT
/	ANALOGOUS PROBLEMS.]  BY PLACING THE OS/8 FILE ON APPROPRIATE DEVICES [SUCH AS
/	DTA1:], THE FILE CAN BE MIGRATED TO P?S/8 USING THE P?S/8 OS8CON [OS/8
/	CONVERSION] UTILITY.  FROM OS/8 IT IS THEN POSSIBLE TO BOOT TO P?S/8 IN THE
/	SAME SESSION, WHERE OS8CON CAN BE RUN AS PART OF A BATCH PROGRAM INCLUDING
/	CREATING AN ASSEMBLY LISTING OF THE FILE PASSED BACK TO THE HOST WINDOWS
/	ENVIRONMENT AS THE OUTPUT OF THE SIMULATED DEVICE 66 LINE PRINTER.  WITH THE
/	AVAILABILITY OF PTUTIL, OS/8 CAN BE COMPLETELY AVOIDED DURING THE DEVELOPMENT
/	PROCESS; P?S/8 BATCH CAN BE RUN AUTOMATICALLY IN AN INFINITE LOOP IF DESIRED
/	[SUCH AS WHEN MAKING FREQUENT EDIT/LISTING CYCLES] IN AN EXTENDED DEVELOPMENT
/	SESSION.  THE ENTIRE PROCESS CAN BE FULLY AUTOMATED OTHER THAN THE REQUIREMENT
/	OF PRESSING CONTROL-E TO EXIT THE SIMH ENVIRONMENT.  [NOTE: UNLIKE OS/8, P?S/8
/	RETAINS THE CURRENT DATE ACROSS REBOOTS.  MOREOVER, P?S/8 SUPPORTS THE TRUE
/	CURRENT DATE WHILE THE OS/8 DATE SUPPORT RAN OUT IN EITHER 1977 OR 2001
/	DEPENDING UPON WHETHER THE OS/8 USER CAN TOLERATE KNOWN KLUDGES THAT DO NOT
/	COMPLETELY FUNCTION.]

/	THUS, WITH THE AVAILABILITY OF PTUTIL, THE PASP ENCOURAGES THE USE OF HOST
/	EDITING AND FILE MAINTENANCE; THE SIMH SIMULATOR IS CALLED UP FOR BRIEF
/	SESSIONS FOR THE PURPOSE OF OBTAINING AN ASSEMBLY LISTING THROUGHOUT THE
/	DEVELOPMENT PROCESS.

/	THE PASP ENCOURAGES THE USE OF HOST EDITING AND FILE MAINTENANCE; THE SIMH
/	SIMULATOR IS CALLED UP FOR BRIEF SESSIONS FOR THE PURPOSE OF OBTAINING AN
/	ASSEMBLY LISTING DURING THE DEVELOPMENT PROCESS; THE PERMANENT COPIES OF
/	SOURCE CODE FILES ARE MAINTAINED IN THE HOST ENVIRONMENT [WINDOWS], NOT IN
/	EITHER P?S/8 OR OS/8.
/	IT IS NECESSARY TO FREELY INTERCHANGE SIMULATED PAPER-TAPE INPUT AND OUTPUT
/	BETWEEN THE SIMH ENVIRONMENT AND THE HOST ENVIRONMENT.  SINCE P?S/8 HAS
/	TRADITIONALLY SHUNNED PAPER-TAPE FOR ALL THE OBVIOUS REASONS GIVEN THE
/	PRESENCE OF STORAGE-BASED OPERATING SYSTEMS, IT DOES NOT PRESENTLY SUPPORT
/	A UTILITY OF THIS NATURE; PTUTIL CAN BE ADDED AS A TEMPORARY SYSTEM PROGRAM
/	[SEE BELOW] TO ALLOW THE DEVELOPMENT MECHANISM DESCRIBED ABOVE.
/	ANYONE WITH ACTUAL PDP-8 HARDWARE DEPENDING ON PAPER-TAPE DATA IS STRONGLY
/	ENCOURAGED TO ABANDON THIS APPROACH IF THEY HAVE SUFFICIENT HARDWARE TO
/	SUPPORT P?S/8.  SINCE MOST P?S/8 CONFIGURATIONS CAN RUN ON A 4K PDP-8 OR NEWER
/	MODEL [EXCEPT FOR THE PDP-8/S DUE TO INCOMPATIBILITY], IT IS RELATIVELY EASY
/	TO COMPLETELY LEAVE THE PAPER-TAPE ENVIRONMENT BEHIND.  [NOTE: PTUTIL ONLY
/	HANDLES ASCII TEXT PAPER-TAPE DATA; P?S/8 BIN CAN HANDLE ALL VARIANTS OF
/	BINARY PAPER-TAPE FORMAT INCLUDING BIN AND RIM FORMAT PAPER-TAPE INPUT AND
/	OUTPUT.]

/	RUNNING PTUTIL IN P?S/8 VERSION 8Z.

/	WHILE PTUTIL CAN BE MANUALLY ADDED TO THE P?S/8 SYSTEMS PROGRAM DIRECTORY, IT
/	WOULD TAKE CONSIDERABLE MANUAL EFFORT TO POSITION IT CLOSER TO THE BEGINNING
/	OF THE SYSTEM DEVICE WITHOUT A MAJOR REORGANIZATION OF THE EXISTING SYSTEM
/	PROGRAMS.  [FORTUNATELY, SUFFICIENT FREE SPACE WAS PROVIDED FOR ADDITION OF
/	SYSTEM PROGRAMS WHEN P?S/8 VERSION 8Z WAS FIRST RELEASED IN 1988.]  AS SUCH,
/	IT IS NOT RECOMMENDED THIS EXPEDIENT METHOD BE USED TO IMPLEMENT PTUTIL ON
/	THIS PARTICULAR P?S/8 RELEASE UNLESS RUNNING UNDER THE SIMH SIMULATOR.  [NOTE:
/	FUTURE P?S/8 RELEASES WILL INCLUDE THE OPTION TO SUPPORT PTUTIL WITH PROPER
/	PROGRAM PLACEMENT.  THOSE KNOWLEDGEABLE OF P?S/8 SYSTEM PROGRAM DIRECTORY
/	PARTICULARS CAN ADD THE PROGRAM AT THE END OF THE CURRENTLY IMPLEMENTED
/	SYSTEM PROGRAMS; ONCE PTUTIL IS STABLE, A PROVISIONAL RE-RELEASE OF P?S/8
/	VERSION 8Z MAY BE PRODUCED.]

/	AS OF VERSION 8Y, P?S/8 INCLUDES THE ABILITY TO SUPPORT A TEMPORARY SYSTEM
/	PROGRAM:

/	.GET BPTUTL				GET THE BINARY FILE[S] OF PTUTIL.
/	.R % [FILES AND COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS]	RUN THE PROGRAM AS % [OR $].

/	THE ONLY RESTRICTION PLACED ON A SYSTEM PROGRAM INITIATED BY THIS MECHANISM IS
/	THE REQUIREMENT OF A STARTING ADDRESS OF 00200 [WHICH IS THE USUAL PROGRAM
/	STARTING ADDRESS FOR MOST PDP-8 PROGRAMMING].  ANY COMBINATION OF COMMAND-LINE
/	OPTION SWITCHES, PASSED INPUT [OR OUTPUT] FILES OR USE OF THE =XXXX IS ALLOWED
/	IN A MANNER IDENTICAL TO PASSING PARAMETERS TO A PERMANENT SYSTEM PROGRAM.

/	[NOTE: IN LIGHT OF THIS MECHANISM, FUTURE RELEASES OF P?S/8 MAY REMOVE CERTAIN
/	SYSTEM PROGRAMS SUCH AS DEVICE FORMATTING PROGRAMS THAT ARE SELDOM USED.  AS
/	SUCH, THEY CAN BE PROVIDED AS BINARY FILES AND AN ACCOMPANYING BATCH FILE TO
/	PERFORM THE EQUIVALENT FUNCTION.  WHERE NECESSARY, THE PROGRAMS CAN BE PATCHED
/	TO ALLOW AN INTERNAL START AT 00200 TO CONFORM WITH THE R % OR $ MECHANISM.
/	USERS CAN MAINTAIN APPROPRIATE UTILITY FILES ON NON-SYSTEM LOGICAL UNITS FOR
/	INFREQUENT ACCESS ALLOWING GENERAL USAGE OF THE SYSTEM DEVICE AT GREATER
/	EFFICIENCY.]
/	PROGRAM EDIT HISTORY.

