/				USING THE PASP VERSION OF THE SIMH SIMULATOR.  TO
/				ENABLE DEBUGGING REQUIRES DE-COMMENTING OF A SINGLE
/				LINE.  DEBUGGING CANNOT BE USED ON DECMATES; THE
/				LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY MUST BE DISABLED.

/	19-NOV-2015	-	DISPLAY PROCESSING APPARENTLY FUNCTIONAL.  WHILE NO
/				SUPPORT YET EXISTS TO CONTROL THE COMMAND-LINE
/				SWITCHES [BECAUSE THE CODE HASN'T BEEN WRITTEN YET],
/				THE DISPLAYED OUTPUT IS NEARLY COMPLETE.  THIS IS
/				EQUIVALENT TO THE '/D' AND '/N' COMMAND-LINE
/				SWITCHES SET WHEN CREATING P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES [WHICH
/				IS NOT IMPLEMENTED YET].  ABOUT 75% OF THE ONCE-ONLY
/				INITIALIZATION CODE IS WRITTEN; THUS, CERTAIN OPTIONS
/				[PARTIALLY] FUNCTION.  [THE OUTPUT HEADER LINE
/				INDICATES THE PROPER CHOICE OF LOW-SPEED OR HIGH-SPEED
/				READER; HOWEVER, THE HIGH-SPEED READER IS THE ONLY
/				FUNCTIONAL INPUT AT THIS TIME.]

/				NEXT TO BE DEVELOPED WILL BE THE ADDITIONAL OPTIONS
/				ASSOCIATED WITH THE VARIOUS DISPLAY MODES [SUCH AS THE
/				'/P' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH] TO ALLOW DETAILED
/				CHANGES TO THE ASSOCIATED CODE.  THE LOW-SPEED READER
/				SUPPORT WILL BE DEFERRED IN THE INTEREST OF GETTING A
/				VIABLE VERSION THAT WILL SUPPORT OUTPUT FILES [WHICH IS
/				THE MOST IMPORTANT FUNCTIONALITY OF PTUTIL].

/				NOTE: EXPECTATIONS OF COPYING SOME OF THIS CODE FROM
/				THE P?S/8 PRINT UTILITY PROVED LESS SUCCESSFUL THAN
/				ORIGINALLY EXPECTED DUE TO THE SOMEWHAT MORE "REAL
/				TIME" NATURE OF PROCESSING PAPER-TAPE DATA ON THE FLY
/				[AS OPPOSED TO PROCESSING CONTENTS OF EXISTING FILES].
/				APPROPRIATE INTERNAL STEERING LOGIC AND CONTROL FLAGS
/				WERE ADDED TO COVER THESE NEW AND DIFFERENT ISSUES.
/	PTUTIL COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS.

/	LIST OF OUTPUT FILES	USED WHEN READING PAPER-TAPE INPUT DATA.  A MAXIMUM OF
/				17 OUTPUT FILES CAN BE CREATED IN A SINGLE SESSION.
/				THE ACTUAL NUMBER OF OUTPUT FILES CREATED WILL BE
/				REPORTED.  [NOTE: WHEN EXTENDED-LENGTH OUTPUT FILES
/				ARE USED, THE MAXIMUM NUMBER OF OUTPUT FILES IS
/				REDUCED TO EIGHT; HOWEVER, DUE TO THE GENERALLY LARGER
/				SIZE OF EXTENDED-LENGTH FILES, IT IS LIKELY THE ENTIRE
/				PAPER-TAPE DATA WITHIN A SINGLE SESSION WILL FIT INTO
/				A SINGLE EXTENDED-LENGTH FILE.]

/	LIST OF INPUT FILES	USED WHEN PUNCHING PAPER-TAPE OUTPUT DATA.

/	/A			AUTOMATIC MODE.  PTUTIL WILL NOT WAIT FOR ANY USER
/				RESPONSES; THIS MODE IS GENERALLY USED FROM FULLY
/				AUTOMATED BATCH SESSIONS TO ALLOW BRIEF SESSIONS OF
/				P?S/8 AS PART OF PROGRAM DEVELOPMENT FROM THE SIMH
/				SIMULATOR.

/	/D			DISPLAY PAPER-TAPE INPUT CHARACTERS.  NOTE: THIS
/				OPTION SHOULD BE USED SPARINGLY WHEN READING FROM
/				THE HIGH-SPEED READER AS THROUGHPUT CAN BE NEGATIVELY
/				IMPACTED.  OTHER OPTION SWITCHES CAN MODIFY THE
/				DISPLAY FORMAT.  [NOTE: ALL INPUT CHARACTERS ARE
/				SUBJECT TO P?S/8 TEXT CONVERSION RULES PRIOR TO
/				DISPLAY.]

/	/E			USE EXTENDED-LENGTH P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES WHEN READING
/				PAPER-TAPE INPUT DATA.  [NOTE: THIS OPTION MUST BE
/				USED CAREFULLY UNTIL P?S/8 IS UPGRADED TO AVOID
/				POTENTIAL TFS FILE DESTRUCTION.  THE CURRENT RELEASE
/				OF PTUTIL IS PROVISIONALLY COMPATIBLE WITH P?S/8
/				VERSION 8Y AND NEWER.  IT IS EXPECTED THAT P?S/8
/				VERSION 9A WILL FULLY SUPPORT EXTENDED-LENGTH FILES
/				CORRECTLY WHICH WILL ELIMINATE THIS RESTRICTION.
/				OTHER THAN THIS WARNING, PTUTIL IS FULLY COMPATIBLE
/				WITH THE INTENTION OF FUTURE RELEASES OF P?S/8; FULLY
/				COMPATIBLE OUTPUT FILE HANDLING WILL BE ADDED TO
/				PTUTIL CONCURRENTLY WITH FUTURE SYSTEM RELEASES.]

/	/F			USE THE HIGH-SPEED READER OR HIGH-SPEED PUNCH INSTEAD
/				OF THE CONSOLE DEVICE FOR PAPER-TAPE INPUT OR OUTPUT.
/	/M			MULTIPLE PAPER-TAPE MODE IS ENABLED.  AT THE END OF
/				THE LATEST PAPER-TAPE, THE USER INDICATES IF FURTHER
/				PAPER-TAPE DATA IS AVAILABLE; CONSOLE INPUT IS
/				REQUIRED [PRESS CONTROL-Z TO CANCEL, ANY OTHER KEY TO
/				PROCEED] TO CONTINUE.  [NOTE: AT THE END OF ANY
/				PAPER-TAPE, THE LATEST LINE OF TEXT WITHIN THE CURRENT
/				OUTPUT FILE IS TERMINATED WITH AN INTERNAL END-OF-LINE
/				SEQUENCE [IF NECESSARY]; HOWEVER, IN MULTIPLE
/				PAPER-TAPE MODE, THE CURRENT OUTPUT FILE REMAINS OPEN
/				TO ALLOW FURTHER PAPER-TAPE INPUT TO BE APPENDED TO
/				THE CURRENT OUTPUT FILE.  ONCE MULTIPLE PAPER-TAPE
/				MODE CONCLUDES, THE CURRENT OUTPUT FILE WILL BE CLOSED
/				IN THE SAME MANNER AS WHEN MULTIPLE PAPER-TAPE MODE IS
/				NOT IN EFFECT.]

/	/N			IF THE '/D' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS SET, INPUT
/				CHARACTERS ARE DISPLAYED WITH FULL PAGINATION
/				INCLUDING TEAR-OFF LINES ORIENTED TOWARDS ROLL PAPER
/				TERMINALS SUCH AS THE TELETYPE MODEL 33.

/	/P			IF THE '/D' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS SET, INPUT
/				CHARACTERS ARE DISPLAYED WILL FULL PAGINATION.  NOTE:
/				THIS OPTION SHOULD ONLY BE USED ON CONSOLE TERMINALS
/				THAT SUPPORT THE FORM-FEED CHARACTER FUNCTION PROPERLY
/				SUCH AS THE TELETYPE MODEL 35 OR DEC LA36 DECWRITER.

/	/Q			CHECK FOR ADDITIONAL FREE SPACE AVAILABLE IN THE
/				CURRENT P?S/8 [TFS] OUTPUT FILE WHEN PROCESSING <FF>
/				CHARACTERS IN THE PAPER-TAPE DATA STREAM.  CERTAIN
/				PROGRAMMING CONVENTIONS EXIST WHERE IT IS DESIRABLE TO
/				AVOID BREAKING THE CONTENTS OF ANY PRINTABLE PAGE [AS
/				DEFINED IN CERTAIN EDITING ENVIRONMENTS AS ALL
/				CHARACTERS CONTAINED BETWEEN <FF> DELIMITING
/				CHARACTERS] IF POSSIBLE.  THIS OPTION IS IGNORED IF
/				THE '/E' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS SET [P?S/8
/				EXTENDED-LENGTH FILES DO NOT REQUIRE INTERNAL FREE
/				SPACE] OR THE '/X' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS SET
/				[WHICH DISABLES SPECIAL <FF> CHARACTER HANDLING].

/	/S			SILENT RUNNING MODE.  THE '/D', '/M' AND '/V'
/				COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES ARE IGNORED; NO MESSAGES
/				ARE ISSUED [OTHER THAN IMPORTANT ERROR MESSAGES].  ALL
/				OTHER REPORTS ARE SUPPRESSED.  PTUTIL WILL RUN IN
/				AUTOMATIC MODE [AS IF THE '/A' COMMAND-LINE OPTION
/				SWITCH WAS SET].

/	/U			CONSOLE REPORT OUTPUT IN UPPER-CASE CHARACTERS; THE
/				DEFAULT IS MIXED UPPER-CASE AND LOWER-CASE OUTPUT.

/	/V			VERBOSE MODE.  VARIOUS CONSOLE MESSAGES ARE
/				EMBELLISHED TO HIGHLIGHT VARIOUS ASPECTS OF THE
/				PROGRAM.  [NOTE: NOT AVAILABLE IN SILENT RUNNING
/				MODE.]
/	/X			DISABLE SPECIAL FORM-FEED PROCESSING.  THIS CAUSES
/				<FF> CHARACTERS READ FROM PAPER-TAPE INPUT TO BECOME
/				THE P?S/8 <EOL> SEQUENCE.

/				WHEN PUNCHING PAPER-TAPE DATA FROM P?S/8 INPUT FILES,
/				THE SEQUENCE <HT> EJECT <EOL> IS PROCESSED LITERALLY
/				INSTEAD OF CONVERSION TO THE <FF> CHARACTER.

/	/2			USE DOUBLE-BUFFERED HIGH-SPEED READER INPUT; THE
/				READER INPUT ROUTINE IS NORMALLY UNBUFFERED.  THIS
/				OPTION SHOULD ONLY BE USED IF THE HIGH-SPEED READER IS
/				PRONE TO TRAILING JUNK CHARACTERS [AND ONLY IF THERE
/				ARE TRAILER FRAMES THAT CAN BE IGNORED].  NOTE: THIS
/				METHOD, WHICH IS ALSO USED IN THE OS/8 PTR: HANDLER,
/				MAY FAIL TO PROCESS THE FINAL PAPER-TAPE FRAME.  DO
/				NOT USE THIS OPTION IF RUNNING P?S/8 ON THE SIMH
/				SIMULATOR AS JUNK CHARACTERS ARE IMPOSSIBLE IN THE
/				SIMH ENVIRONMENT.  NOTE: THE /2 OPTION SWITCH IS
/				IGNORED IF THE LOW-SPEED TELETYPE MODEL 33 ASR OR 35
/				ASR TERMINAL IS USED FOR PAPER-TAPE INPUT; THE /F
/				OPTION SWITCH WILL NOT BE SET.  [THIS OPTION IS
/				IGNORED IF PUNCHING PAPER-TAPE DATA FROM P?S/8 INPUT
/				FILES.]

/	/8			PTUTIL WILL EXIT BY EXECUTION OF THE 6050 INSTRUCTION
/				WHICH TERMINATES SUITABLY CONFIGURED SIMH SIMULATOR
/				SESSIONS.  [NOTE: THE PROGRAM WILL ALSO EXIT TO P?S/8
/				IN THE USUAL MANNER IN CASE THIS FEATURE IS NOT
/				SUPPORTED.]

/	=XXXX			OVERRIDE THE DEFAULT LEADER/TRAILER OUTPUT FRAME COUNT
/				OF 100 DECIMAL [144 OCTAL].  [NOTE: ATTEMPTS TO USE A
/				LEADER/TRAILER OUTPUT FRAME COUNT OF LESS THAN 7 OR
/				LARGER THAN 400 (DECIMAL 256) WILL BE IGNORED.]

/	NOTE: FUTURE RELEASES MAY DEFINE ADDITIONAL COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS.
/	PROGRAM MESSAGES.

/	PAPER-TAPE => P?S/8

/				PAPER-TAPE DATA WILL BE OBTAINED FROM THE PREVAILING
/				PAPER-TAPE READER AND WRITTEN TO P?S/8 TFS FILE[S].
/				THIS INDICATES P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES ARE SPECIFIED; THE
/				'/E' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS NOT SET.

/	PAPER-TAPE => P?S/8 [EXTENDED FILES]

/				PAPER-TAPE DATA WILL BE OBTAINED FROM THE PREVAILING
/				PAPER-TAPE READER AND WRITTEN TO P?S/8 EXTENDED-LENGTH
/				FILE[S].  THIS INDICATES P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES ARE
/				SPECIFIED; THE '/E' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS SET.
/	COMMAND ERROR MESSAGES.

/	CANNOT COMBINE INPUT FILES *AND* OUTPUT FILES!

/		AN ATTEMPT WAS MADE TO RUN PTUTIL WITH BOTH INPUT AND OUTPUT FILES.
/		PTUTIL CAN ONLY BE USED WITH INPUT FILES OR OUTPUT FILES BUT NOT BOTH
/		TYPES OF FILES AT THE SAME TIME.

/	NO FILES!

/		AN ATTEMPT WAS MADE TO RUN PTUTIL WITHOUT PASSING ANY FILES.  PTUTIL
/		CAN ONLY BE USED WITH INPUT [OR OUTPUT] FILES [BUT NOT BOTH AT THE
/		SAME TIME].

/	ONE OR MORE INPUT FILES ARE DUPLICATES!

/		AN INPUT FILE WAS DETECTED THAT IS A DUPLICATE OF ANOTHER INPUT FILE.
/		ALL INPUT FILES USED WITH PTUTIL MUST BE UNIQUE.

/	ONE OR MORE OUTPUT FILES ARE DUPLICATES!

/		AN OUTPUT FILE WAS DETECTED THAT IS A DUPLICATE OF ANOTHER OUTPUT
/		FILE.  ALL OUTPUT FILES USED WITH PTUTIL MUST BE UNIQUE.
/	SPECIAL CONTROL CHARACTERS.

/	<BRK>

/	IF THE <BRK> KEY IS PRESSED DURING PROGRAM OPERATION, THE PROGRAM ABORTS AND
/	EXITS TO 07600 TO REBOOT P?S/8.  THIS WILL NOT AFFECT BATCH OPERATIONS [IF
/	APPLICABLE].

/	CONTROL-A

/	IF THE CONTROL-A KEY IS PRESSED DURING PROGRAM OPERATION, THE PROGRAM ABORTS
/	AND EXITS TO 07600 TO REBOOT P?S/8.  THIS WILL NOT AFFECT BATCH OPERATIONS
/	[IF APPLICABLE].

/	CONTROL-B

/	IF THE CONTROL-B KEY IS PRESSED DURING PROGRAM OPERATION, THE PROGRAM ABORTS
/	AND EXITS TO 07600 TO REBOOT P?S/8.  THIS WILL NOT AFFECT BATCH OPERATIONS [IF
/	APPLICABLE].

/	CONTROL-C

/	IF THE CONTROL-C KEY IS PRESSED DURING PROGRAM OPERATION, THE PROGRAM ABORTS
/	AND EXITS TO 07600 TO REBOOT P?S/8.  BATCH OPERATIONS WILL ALSO BE ABORTED [IF
/	APPLICABLE].

/	CONTROL-O

/	IF THE CONTROL-O KEY IS PRESSED, THE CURRENT STATE OF OUTPUT DISPLAY IS
/	INVERTED.  "^O" WILL BE PRINTED TO ACKNOWLEDGE THE CHANGE OF DISPLAY STATE.

/	CONTROL-S

/	IF CONTROL-S IS DETECTED ON THE CONSOLE INPUT DEVICE, THE PROGRAM WAITS UNTIL
/	CONTROL-Q IS DETECTED ON THE CONSOLE INPUT DEVICE BEFORE FURTHER CONSOLE
/	OUTPUT [IF ANY].

/	WHILE WAITING FOR CONTROL-Q, ALL CONTROL CHARACTERS THAT CAN ABORT THE PROGRAM
/	ARE ACTIVE.  [NOTE: DEPENDING ON THE EXACT CONSOLE DEVICE, CONTROL-S AND
/	CONTROL-Q MAY BE AUTOMATICALLY GENERATED BY THE TERMINAL AS PART OF STANDARD
/	FLOW-CONTROL PROTOCOL MECHANISMS OR FUNCTION KEYS.]
/	PAPER-TAPE INPUT FORMAT.

/	1)	LEADER SECTION.

/		WHILE OPTIONAL [BECAUSE TOTAL COMPLIANCE CANNOT BE FORCED], THIS IS
/		A SECTION OF PAPER-TAPE FRAMES WITH THE HIGH-BIT ONLY PUNCHED.  THE
/		LEADER SECTION CAN BE ANY CONVENIENT LENGTH [OR LENGTH ZERO].  PTUTIL
/		INITIALLY IS PLACED IN THE LEADER DETECTION MODE AS ALL LEADER FRAMES
/		ARE IGNORED.

/	2)	DATA SECTION.

/		THIS IS THE ACTIVE TEXTUAL DATA SECTION OF THE PAPER-TAPE.  FAILING TO
/		OBTAIN THIS SECTION WILL RESULT IN AN ERROR MESSAGE REGARDING THE LACK
/		OF INPUT DATA.  ALL DATA VALUES ARE ALLOWED EXCEPT A LEADER/TRAILER
/		FRAME [WHICH WOULD SIGNAL THE END OF THE DATA SECTION].  ALL PARITY
/		BITS ARE REMOVED BEFORE ANY FURTHER CHARACTER FILTERING FOR PROCESSING
/		INTO THE CONTENTS OF P?S/8 TEXTUAL OUTPUT FILES.

/	3)	TRAILER SECTION.

/		WHILE OPTIONAL [BECAUSE TOTAL COMPLIANCE CANNOT BE FORCED], THIS IS
/		GENERALLY A SECTION CONSISTING OF PAPER-TAPE FRAMES WITH ONLY THE
/		HIGH-BIT PUNCHED.  WHILE ANY CONVENIENT LENGTH MAY BE PRESENT, ONLY
/		THE FIRST TRAILER FRAME IS READ.  ASSUMING THE MULTIPLE INPUT TAPE
/		MODE ['/M' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS SET] IS IN EFFECT, THE
/		TRAILER WILL BE CONSIDERED THE LEADER SECTION DURING A
/		SUBSEQUENT READ OPERATION [UNLESS THE TAPE IS REPOSITIONED].

/	NOTE: IF THE DATA SECTION TERMINATES WITH THE CONTROL-Z CHARACTER, THE REST OF
/	THE DATA SECTION [IF ANY] AND THE ENTIRE TRAILER SECTION [IF ANY] ARE IGNORED.
/	IF THE MULTIPLE INPUT TAPE MODE IS IN EFFECT, THE USER MAY HAVE TO REPOSITION
/	THE TAPE IN THE READER TO AVOID JUNK [OR ALLOW THE JUNK CHARACTERS TO BE
/	PROCESSED WHICH MAY REQUIRE SUBSEQUENT MANUAL FILE EDITING].  [THE STANDARD
/	PAPER-TAPE FORMAT, WHICH IS CREATED BY PTUTIL WHEN PUNCHING PAPER-TAPE OUTPUT
/	DATA, CONSISTS OF A LEADER SECTION, A DATA SECTION TERMINATED BY CONTROL-Z AND
/	A TRAILER SECTION.  STANDARD FORMAT TAPES WILL ALWAYS BE READ CORRECTLY AND
/	COMPLETELY.  IF MULTIPLE STANDARD FORMAT TAPES ARE BEING READ, THE USER MUST
/	CHANGE PAPER-TAPES WHEN DIRECTED.]

/	THIS FORMAL DEFINITION OF PROPER PAPER-TAPE INPUT ALLOWS STANDARD TAPES TO BE
/	READ WITH EASE, YET ALLOWS NON-STANDARD INPUT TO BE READ, ALBEIT WITH SOME
/	NEED TO DO FOLLOW-UP EDITING AS REQUIRED.

/	FOR EXAMPLE, CERTAIN PAPER-TAPES WERE CREATED DURING FOCAL INPUT SESSIONS THAT
/	HAVE THE "*" PROMPT OF FOCAL STARTING EVERY LINE.  [THESE TAPES WERE GENERALLY
/	PRODUCED BY ENABLING THE PAPER-TAPE PUNCH ON TELETYPE MODEL 33 ASR OR 35 ASR
/	CONSOLE TERMINALS DURING THE ORIGINAL ENTRY OF THE FOCAL PROGRAM INTO THE
/	STANDALONE PAPER-TAPE RELEASE OF FOCAL, 1969 OR OTHER VERSIONS.]
/	AFTER USING PTUTIL TO TRANSFER THE PAPER-TAPE DATA TO P?S/8 TEXT FILES,
/	FOLLOW-UP EDITING CAN BE PERFORMED TO REMOVE THE "*" CHARACTERS.  [NOTE: AN
/	IMPERFECT SOLUTION TO THIS PROBLEM CAN BE ACHIEVED WITH THE KEYBOARD MONITOR
/	"CHANGE" COMMAND.  WHEN THE '/A' OPTION SWITCH IS USED, ALL OCCURRENCES OF THE
/	"*" CHARACTER CAN BE REMOVED; THIS WILL INCLUDE "*" CHARACTERS POTENTIALLY
/	USED IN THE BODY OF THE FOCAL STATEMENTS THAT MUST BE PRESERVED.  A COPY OF
/	THE FILE SHOULD BE LISTED OUT OR PRINTED WITH THE P?S/8 "PRINT" COMMAND TO
/	LOCATE THIS INCIDENTAL EXCESSIVE CHARACTER REMOVAL FOR MANUAL RESTORATION
/	AFTER ALL AUTOMATIC OPERATIONS HAVE CONCLUDED.]

/	NOTE: PAPER-TAPES CREATED BY LISTING THE FOCAL PROGRAM USING THE FOCAL "W"
/	COMMAND ARE UNAFFECTED BY THIS ANOMALY; THE STATEMENTS WILL BE PROPERLY STORED
/	AS INTENDED [FOCAL DOES NOT INCLUDE THE "*" PROMPT IN THE LISTING CREATED BY
/	THIS COMMAND].

/	LOW-SPEED READER CONSIDERATIONS.

/	WHEN THE LOW-SPEED PAPER-TAPE READER IS SELECTED [WHICH GENERALLY APPLIES ONLY
/	TO TELETYPE MODEL 33 ASR OR 35 ASR CONSOLE TERMINALS], CERTAIN RESTRICTIONS
/	WILL BE IN EFFECT DURING PAPER-TAPE READ OPERATIONS:

/	1) THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY WILL NOT BE USED; ALL INPUT [AND OUTPUT] IS
/	   DIRECTED TO THE PHYSICAL CONSOLE DEVICE.  [NOTE: IF APPLICABLE, THE
/	   PAPER-TAPE READ SESSION WILL BE INITIATED BY PRESSING ANY KEY ON THE
/	   LOGICAL CONSOLE KEYBOARD INPUT DEVICE.]

/	2) THE CONSOLE INPUT WILL BE SUBJECT TO A TIME-OUT.  FAILING TO OBTAIN CONSOLE
/	   INPUT CHARACTERS WILL RESULT IN CLOSING THE INPUT DEVICE FOR DATA PURPOSES.

/	3) DUE TO HARDWARE RESTRICTIONS, IT WILL NOT BE POSSIBLE TO CHANGE THE
/	   OPERATION OF THE PROGRAM WITH REGARD TO ANY OF THE NORMALLY SUPPORTED
/	   CONTROL CHARACTER FUNCTIONS [<BRK>, CONTROL-A, CONTROL-B, CONTROL-C,
/	   CONTROL-S/CONTROL-Q AND CONTROL-O]; ATTEMPTS TO USE KEYBOARD INPUT MAY
/	   GARBLE THE INPUT DATA.
/	NUMERIC LOAD DEFINITIONS.

	NL0001=	CLA IAC			/LOAD AC WITH 0001.
	NL0002=	CLA CLL CML RTL		/LOAD AC WITH 0002
	NL0010=	CLA IAC RAL RAR		/LOAD AC WITH 0010 [ON 6120 CPU ONLY].
	NL2000=	CLA CLL CML RTR		/LOAD AC WITH 2000.
	NL4000=	CLA CLL CML RAR		/LOAD AC WITH 4000.
	NL7775=	CLA CLL CMA RTL		/LOAD AC WITH 7775.
	NL7777=	CLA CMA			/LOAD AC WITH 7777.

/	P?S/8 DEFINITIONS.

	BSGRP=	0006			/CURRENT BASE YEAR GROUP VALUE.
	INCON=	0031			/LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY INPUT ROUTINE.
	OUTCON=	0033			/LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY OUTPUT ROUTINE.
	SBOOT=	7600			/P?S/8 GENERAL RESTART ADDRESS.
	SCRSIZE=7611			/CORE SIZE, OVERLAY AND LOGICAL ABORT WORD.
	SDATE=	7610			/SYSTEM [IN MEMORY] DATE WORD.
	SFILES=	7757			/PASSED FILE LIST POINTER.
	SOUTFLS=7607			/OUTPUT FILE COUNT IN BITS[7-11].
	SWAL=	7604			/PASSED OPTION SWITCHES /A-/L.
	SWMX=	7605			/PASSED OPTION SWITCHES /M-/X.
	SWY9=	7606			/PASSED OPTION SWITCHES /Y-/9.

/	HIGH-SPEED READER/PUNCH DEFINITIONS.

	PCF=	6022			/HIGH-SPEED PUNCH CLEAR DONE FLAG.
	PLS=	6026			/HIGH-SPEED PUNCH OUTPUT FRAME AND CLEAR FLAG.
	PPC=	6024			/HIGH-SPEED PUNCH OUTPUT FRAME.
	PSF=	6021			/HIGH-SPEED PUNCH SKIP ON DONE FLAG.
	RFC=	6014			/READER FETCH CHARACTER AND CLEAR FLAG.
	RRB=	6012			/HIGH-SPEED READER READ BUFFER AND CLEAR FLAG.
	RSF=	6011			/HIGH-SPEED READER SKIP ON FRAME AVAILABLE.

/	ADDITIONAL DEFINITIONS.

	DECIMAL				/MAKE IT EASIER.

	DFRMCNT=100			/DEFAULT LEADER/TRAILER OUTPUT FRAME COUNT.
	EXTRA=	5			/EXTRA LINE COUNT ON A 66 LINE PAGE.
	LINES=	55			/PRINTED CONTENT LINE COUNT ON A 66 LINE PAGE.

	OCTAL				/BACK TO OCTAL.

	OUTIME=	140			/OUTER COUNT FOR LOW-SPEED READER TIME-OUT.
	REVISIO="A&77			/PROGRAM REVISION.
	VERSION=1			/PROGRAM VERSION.

/	DEBUGGING.  [NOTE: FOR PDP-8 [NOT DECMATE] WITH LOGICAL CONSOLE DISABLED.]

	DEBUG=	1			/DEBUGGING IS ENABLED IF THIS IS NOT A COMMENT.

	IFNDEF	DEBUG	<DEBUG=	0>	/NOT DEBUGGING BY DEFAULT.
	PAGE	0			/START AT THE BEGINNING.

	*10				/GET TO AUTO-INDEX AREA.

XR0,	.-.				/AUTO-INDEX REGISTER 0.
XR1,	.-.				/AUTO-INDEX REGISTER 1.
XR2,	.-.				/AUTO-INDEX REGISTER 2.

	*20				/GET PAST AUTO-INDEX AREA.

COLUMN,	.-.				/OUTPUT COLUMN COUNTER.
CONLATE,.-.				/LATEST CONSOLE INPUT CHARACTER.
INCNTL,	.-.				/LOW-ORDER FRAME COUNTER.
INCNTH,	.-.				/HIGH-ORDER FRAME COUNTER.
INFLAG,	.-.				/PAPER-TAPE INPUT CONTROL FLAG.
INTEMP,	.-.				/PAPER-TAPE INPUT TEMPORARY.
FRMCNT,	-DFRMCNT			/LEADER/TRAILER OUTPUT FRAME COUNT.
LINCNT,	.-.				/OUTPUT LINE COUNTER.
LINE,	.-.				/OUTPUT LINE.
OUTCHAR,.-.				/OUTPUT TEMPORARY.
OUTCNT,	.-.				/PASSED OUTPUT FILE COUNT.
OUTHDFL,.-.				/OUTPUT HEADER FLAG.
PSXTMP,	.-.				/PASSED VALUE SAVED HERE FOR PSXBIT ROUTINE.
PTLATES,.-.				/LATEST PAPER-TAPE CHARACTER PROCESSED.
PTPREVI,.-.				/PREVIOUS PAPER-TAPE CHARACTER PROCESSED.
RTIMER,	.-.				/READER TIME-OUT COUNTER.
TCNTLOW,0				/LOW-ORDER TOTAL FRAME COUNT.
TCNTHIG,0				/HIGH-ORDER TOTAL FRAME COUNT.

	PAGE	1			/THE USUAL STARTING ADDRESS.

/	THE PROGRAM STARTS HERE FOR COMPATIBILITY WITH THE R % OR R $ MECHANISM.

PTUTIL,	NOP				/IN CASE CHAINED TO.
	JMP I	(PTINIT)		/PROGRAM STARTUP ADDRESS.

/	OVERALL PROGRAM MEMORY LAYOUT CONSIDERATIONS.

/	ALL CODE AND DATA USED TO CREATE P?S/8 TFS OUTPUT FILES FROM PAPER-TAPE MUST
/	BE LOADED FIRST AND LOADED INTO 00000-02777 [OR LESS].  ALL ADDITIONAL CODE TO
/	CREATE P?S/8 EXTENDED-LENGTH OUTPUT FILES CAN FOLLOW THIS SECTION OF THE
/	PROGRAM [INCLUDING ERROR MESSAGES SPECIFIC TO EXTENDED-LENGTH OUTPUT FILE
/	CREATION].  DEPENDING ON PROGRAM COMPLEXITY, THE SECTION REQUIRED FOR CREATING
/	EXTENDED-LENGTH OUTPUT FILES CAN BE DESIGNATED AS AN OVERLAY TO ANY AREA OF
/	MEMORY PURELY INVOLVED IN CREATING TFS FILES [WITH APPROPRIATE ONCE-ONLY
/	INITIALIZATION CODE] AS THESE ROUTINES ARE MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE.

/	ALL ONCE-ONLY INITIALIZATION CODE ROUTINES AND MESSAGES ARE LOADED BEYOND
/	THESE AREAS.  THE ONLY OVERALL REQUIREMENT IS FITTING THE ENTIRE PROGRAM INTO
/	00000-07577.  ALL SECTIONS OF THE PROGRAM SHOULD BE SUFFICIENTLY OPTIMIZED TO
/	PREVENT THE OVERALL PROGRAM FROM BECOMING LARGER THAN NECESSARY [IN TERMS OF
/	ENTIRE PAGES OF MEMORY USED FOR INITIAL LOADING BY P?S/8].

FRMSMSG,TEXT	" ^F^RAMES"		/FRAME[S] MESSAGE.
INEOFME,TEXT	"%^N^O ^I^NPUT!%"	/NO INPUT MESSAGE.
RDMSG,	TEXT	" ^R^EAD%^"		/READ MESSAGE.
/	GET AND PROCESS PAPER-TAPE INPUT [CALLED AS A SUBROUTINE FOR NOW].

INTAPE,	.-.				/GET AND PROCESS PAPER-TAPE INPUT ROUTINE.
	NL0001				/SET A NON-ZERO VALUE
	DCA	RTIMER			/SETUP TIME-OUT COUNT.
	DCA	INFLAG			/INITIAL STATE - NO LEADER FRAMES NOR INPUT YET.
	DCA	INCNTLOW		/CLEAR LOW-ORDER FRAME COUNT.
	DCA	INCNTHIGH		/CLEAR HIGH-ORDER FRAME COUNT.
	JMS	HGET			/TRY TO GET AN INITIAL CHARACTER
	JMP	INEOF			/WASN'T ANY [OR CONTROL-Z FOUND], GO FINISH.
	JMP	INLENTRY		/DON'T NEED ANOTHER ONE [YET].

INLOOP,	JMS	HGET			/GET A CHARACTER.
	JMP	COUNTIN			/NO FURTHER INPUT [OR CONTROL-Z FOUND].
INLENTR,ISZ	INCNTLOW		/BUMP LOW-ORDER FRAME COUNT.
	SKP				/DON'T BUMP HIGH-ORDER UNLESS IT OVERFLOWED.
	ISZ	INCNTHIGH		/BUMP HIGH-ORDER FRAME COUNT.
	TAD	[-200]			/COMPARE TO STANDARD LEADER FRAME.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF A LEADER FRAME.
	JMP	NOTLDR			/JUMP IF NOT.

/	LEADER FRAME FOUND; ARE WE EXPECTING IT?

	TAD	INFLAG			/GET THE INPUT CONTROL FLAG.
	SZA				/SKIP IF TOSSING LEADER FRAMES.
	JMP	INEOF			/TRAILER FRAME FOUND, WE'RE DONE.

/	WE ARE [STILL] IGNORING LEADER FRAMES.

	JMP	INLOOP			/GO GET ANOTHER FRAME.
/	COMES HERE IF NOT A LEADER FRAME.

NOTLDR,	TAD	INTEMP			/GET THE LATEST FRAME.
	AND	[177]			/JUST ASCII TEXT BITS.
	SNA				/SKIP IF ACTUAL DATA.
	JMP	INLOOP			/IGNORE PURE <NUL> FRAMES.
	ISZ	INFLAG			/SET DATA MODE; 200 READ IS NOW A TRAILER FRAME.
	SKP				/DON'T SET IT TWICE.
	ISZ	INFLAG			/EVERY 4096 FRAMES, COMES HERE TO MAKE SURE.
	JMS I	(PQSOUT)		/PROCESS AS P?S/8 FILE CHARACTER.
	JMP	 INLOOP			/KEEP GOING.

/	COMES HERE WHEN THERE IS NO [FURTHER] INPUT.

INEOF,	TAD	INCNTLOW		/GET LOW-ORDER FRAME COUNT.
	SNA				/SKIP IF SOME.
	TAD	INCNTHIGH		/GET HIGH-ORDER FRAME COUNT.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF THERE WERE NO DATA FRAMES.
	JMP	COUNTIN			/JUMP AROUND MESSAGE PRINT IF THERE WERE SOME.
	JMS I	(SCRIBE)		/COMPLAIN OF
	INEOFMESSAGE			/NO INPUT.

/	COMES HERE TO REPORT THE PROCESSED FRAME COUNT.

COUNTIN,JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.

/	CHECK FOR EXACTLY ONE FRAME; IF SO, CHANGE THE MESSAGE.

	TAD	INCNTHIGH		/GET HIGH-ORDER HALF.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF ZERO.
	JMP	JUSTPRT			/PRINT PLURAL IF LARGE NON-ZERO.
	NL7777				/SET -1.
	TAD	INCNTLOW		/CHECK IF LOW-ORDER IS EXACTLY 0001.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF SO.
JUSTPRT,TAD	("S^100)		/PUT THE PLURAL FORM IN THE MESSAGE.
	DCA	FRMSMSG+4		/STORE EITHER WAY. 
	JMS I	(DPRINT)		/CALL DOUBLE-PRECISION PRINT ROUTINE.
	INCNTLOW			/POINTER TO LOW-ORDER HALF OF ARGUMENT.
	JMS I	(SCRIBE)		/CALL MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE
	FRMSMSG				/TO PRINT FRAME[S] MESSAGE.
	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/CALL MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE.
	RDMSG				/TO PRINT READ MESSAGE.

/	NOTE: OPEN P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES NEED TO BE CLOSED AT THE CALLER'S CONTEXT!

	JMP I	INTAPE			/RETURN.
/	ROUTINE TO GET A CHARACTER FROM THE HIGH-SPEED READER.

/	CALL WITH:

/	JMS	HGET			/CALL ROUTINE.
/	END-OF-INPUT			/COMES HERE IF NO INPUT AVAILABLE [CONTROL-Z].
/	GOT-A-CHARACTER			/SKIP RETURN IF NOT CONTROL-Z.

HGET,	.-.				/GET A CHARACTER FROM THE HIGH-SPEED READER.
	JMS I	(HIREAD)		/CALL THE HIGH-SPEED READER INPUT ROUTINE.
	DCA	INTEMP			/SAVE THE LATEST CHARACTER.
	TAD	INTEMP			/GET IT BACK.
	AND	[177]			/JUST ASCII BITS.
	TAD	(-"Z!300)		/COMPARE TO CONTROL-Z.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF OTHER THAN CONTROL-Z.
	JMP I	HGET			/TAKE IMMEDIATE RETURN IF NO [FURTHER] INPUT.
	ISZ	HGET			/BUMP PAST END-OF-INPUT ADDRESS.
	TAD	INTEMP			/GET THE LATEST CHARACTER BACK.
	JMP I	HGET			/SKIP RETURN TO CALLER.

/	NOTE:  ALL OF THE PROGRAM CODE ABOVE [ON THIS PAGE] IS OBSOLESCENT AND WILL
/	BE REMOVED; IT WAS USED IN AN EARLY DEVELOPMENT VERSION TO TEST CERTAIN
/	ROUTINES INDEPENDENTLY [AND TO DEVELOP OTHER ROUTINES THAT REPLACE THESE
/	ROUTINES.]  THE TEXT MESSAGES WILL BE RELOCATED AT THAT TIME AS WELL, ETC.

	PAGE				/DUMP LITERALS NOW.
/	COMES HERE IF CREATING P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES FROM PAPER-TAPE INPUT DATA.

OUTFILE,JMS I	(PQINITIALIZE)		/INITIALIZE P?S/8 OUTPUT FILE STREAM.
MORETAP,JMS I	RDRINITIALIZE		/INITIALIZE THE PAPER-TAPE INPUT DEVICE.

/	SINCE DOUBLE-BUFFERED HIGH-SPEED READER HANDLING MAY BE IN EFFECT, CHECK NOW
/	TO DETERMINE IF THERE IS NO VIABLE INPUT.

	JMS	RDRGET			/TRY TO GET AN INITIAL READER FRAME.
	JMP	PTEOF			/WASN'T ANY [OR CONTROL-Z FOUND], GO FINISH UP.
	JMP	PTGOT1			/GOT ONE, CONTINUE THERE WITH LATEST IN THE AC.

/	COMES HERE TO ATTEMPT TO GET SUBSEQUENT CHARACTERS.

RDRLOOP,JMS	RDRGET			/TRY TO GET ADDITIONAL INPUT FRAMES.
	JMP	PTEOF			/NOTHING FURTHER, GO FINISH UP.

/	FALLS THROUGH WITH LATEST FRAME IN THE AC.

/	JMP	PTGOT1			/CONTINUE THERE.

/	COMES HERE IF WE HAVE SOME INPUT FRAMES WITH LATEST FRAME IN THE AC.

PTGOT1,	ISZ	INCNTLOW		/BUMP LATEST TAPE'S LOW-ORDER FRAME COUNT.
	SKP				/DON'T BUMP HIGH-ORDER UNLESS IT OVERFLOWED.
	ISZ	INCNTHIGH		/BUMP LATEST TAPE'S HIGH-ORDER FRAME COUNT.
	ISZ	TCNTLOW			/BUMP LOW-ORDER OVERALL FRAME COUNT.
	SKP				/DON'T BUMP HIGH-ORDER UNLESS IT OVERFLOWED.
	ISZ	TCNTHIGH		/BUMP HIGH-ORDER OVERALL FRAME COUNT.
	TAD	[-200]			/COMPARE TO STANDARD LEADER FRAME VALUE.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF A STANDARD LEADER FRAME.
	JMP	NOTLEADER		/JUMP IF NOT.

/	LEADER/TRAILER FRAME FOUND; WHICH IS IT?

	TAD	INFLAG			/GET THE INPUT CONTROL FLAG.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF TOSSING LEADER FRAMES CURRENTLY.
	JMP	PTEOF			/TRAILER FRAME FOUND; WE'RE DONE.

/	LEADER FRAME FOUND; IGNORE IT AND KEEP GOING.

	JMP	RDRLOOP			/GO GET ANOTHER ONE.

/	COMES HERE IF LATEST IS NOT A LEADER FRAME.

NOTLEAD,TAD	INTEMP			/GET THE LATEST FRAME VALUE.
	AND	[177]			/IGNORE PARITY BIT.
	DCA	PTLATEST		/SAVE AS OUR LATEST CHARACTER.
	TAD	PTLATEST		/GET IT BACK.
	SNA				/SKIP IF <NUL> VALUE.
	JMP	RDRLOOP			/IGNORE <NUL> FRAMES AND KEEP GOING.
	ISZ	INFLAG			/SET DATA FOUND MODE; 200 CODE IS NOW TRAILER.
	SKP				/DON'T SET IT TWICE.
	ISZ	INFLAG			/THIS HAPPENS EVERY 4096 FRAMES ARE READ.
/	WE MUST FILTER OUT AND/OR CONVERT ALL SEVEN-BIT ASCII CHARACTERS TO P?S/8
/	SIXBIT:

/	 1)  CONTROL CHARACTERS IN GENERAL ARE IGNORED [OTHER THAN THE SPECIFIC
/	     SPECIAL CASES NOTED BELOW].  THESE CHARACTERS COULD BE LOCATED WITHIN
/	     SEQUENCES SUCH AS <CR>/<LF> INTENDED AS FILLER CHARACTERS.

/	 2)  CODE 015 <CR> BECOMES THE P?S/8 <EOL> CHARACTER.

/	 3)  CODE 012 <LF> IS IGNORED IF AFTER <CR>.  OTHERWISE IT BECOMES THE P?S/8
/	     <EOL> CHARACTER.  THIS ALLOWS STRINGS OF <LF> CHARACTERS TO BECOME NULL
/	     LINES [WITH LINE NUMBERS WHERE APPLICABLE] AS IF A SERIES OF <CR>/<LF>
/	     CHARACTER PAIRS.  THE ORIGINAL INTENTION CANNOT BE EXACTLY DUPLICATED
/	     WITHIN P?S/8 TEXT FILES; HOWEVER, DEPENDING ON THE LANGUAGE PROCESSING
/	     PROGRAM [SUCH AS P?S/8 PAL] USED, THE INTENDED FUNCTION WILL GENERALLY BE
/	     PRODUCED.

/	 4)  CODE 011 <HT> BECOMES P?S/8 CODE 37 WHICH IS THE INTERNAL CODE FOR <HT>.

/	 5)  CODE 014 <FF> IS HANDLED FOR '/D' COMMAND LINE OPTION [DISPLAY] PURPOSES
/	     AS A <FF> [POSSIBLY SIMULATED OR OTHERWISE PADDED OUT DEPENDING ON THE
/	     CONSOLE DEVICE CAPABILITIES].  WITHIN THE ACTUAL FILE, <FF> IS EITHER
/	     CONVERTED TO <EOL> ALONE OR EXPANDED TO <HT> EJECT <EOL> DEPENDING ON
/	     OTHER COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS.  <FF> DISPLAY MAY ALSO BE OUTPUT AS LITERALLY
/	     "<FF>" [SURROUNDED BY <CR>/<LF> CHARACTERS TO MAKE IT CLEAR THE
/	     <FF> WAS DETECTED IN THE INPUT STREAM]; THIS MODE APPLIES IF THE '/D'
/	     COMMAND LINE SWITCH IS SET WITHOUT THE '/N' OR '/P' SWITCHES SET.  THESE
/	     OPTIONS CAN FURTHER CHANGE OUTPUT SPECIFICS.

/	 6)  CODE 032 CONTROL-Z IS THE END-OF-FILE INDICATOR.  THIS DATA COULD
/	     ACTUALLY BE PART OF THE INPUT STREAM, OR COULD BE SIGNALLED BY EITHER
/	     DETECTION OF A TRAILER FRAME OR INPUT DEVICE TIME-OUT.  THE LATEST LINE
/	     IN THE FILE WILL BE TERMINATED WITH <EOL> IF NECESSARY AND THE DATA
/	     OPERATION IS CLOSED UNLESS THE MULTIPLE INPUT TAPE MODE ['/M'
/	     COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS SET] IS IN EFFECT.  ASSUMING MULTIPLE INPUT
/	     TAPES ARE PROCESSED, EVENTUALLY THE LATEST OPEN FILE WILL BE CLOSED ON
/	     CONTROL-Z DETECTION; FINAL REPORTS ON OUTPUT FILE CREATION ARE ISSUED
/	     JUST PRIOR TO PROGRAM EXIT.

/	 7)  CODE 100 <AT-SIGN> AND CODE 140 <ACCENT-MARK> CHARACTERS ARE IGNORED.
/	     HOWEVER, THESE CHARACTERS INTERACT WITH THE LOGIC REGARDING DISPOSITION
/	     OF THE <LF> CHARACTER SINCE IN CERTAIN SITUATIONS THEY ARE CONSIDERED
/	     PRINTING CHARACTERS [WHICH CANNOT BE EXPRESSED IN P?S/8 TEXT FILES].

/	 8)  ALL OTHER LOWER-CASE PRINTING CHARACTERS ARE CONVERTED ["FOLDED"] TO THE
/	     CORRESPONDING UPPER-CASE EQUIVALENT.  THE SIX-BIT REPRESENTATION IS
/	     PLACED INTO THE P?S/8 TEXT FILE.
/	 9)  CODE 137 [<LEFT-ARROW> ON CERTAIN TERMINALS, <UNDERLINE> ON OTHERS] IS
/	     NOT USED IN P?S/8 TEXT FILES.  IN THE P?S/8 KEYBOARD MONITOR, THIS CODE
/	     IS GENERALLY TREATED AS AN ALTERNATIVE TO THE <RO>, <BS> OR <DEL> KEY.

/	10)  CODE 175 [<RIGHT-BRACE>] IS SOMETIMES AVAILABLE ON CERTAIN TERMINALS AS
/	     AN ALTERNATE TO THE 033 <ESC> CODE; KEYBOARD MONITOR SETTINGS CAN
/	     DESIGNATE THIS CODE AS THE <ESC> CHARACTER IF REQUIRED.  FOR TERMINALS
/	     THAT CAN ISSUE THIS CODE, IT COULD BE CONTAINED IN PAPER-TAPE DATA, IN
/	     WHICH CASE IT WILL BE TREATED AS A LOWER-CASE CHARACTER TRANSLATED TO "]"
/	     DEPENDING ON SPECIFIC TERMINAL CHARACTERISTICS.

/	11)  CODE 176 [<TILDE] IS SOMETIMES AVAILABLE ON CERTAIN TERMINALS AS AN
/	     ALTERNATE TO THE 033 <ESC> CODE; KEYBOARD MONITOR SETTINGS CAN DESIGNATE
/	     THIS CODE AS THE <ESC> CHARACTER IF REQUIRED.  FOR TERMINALS THAT CAN
/	     ISSUE  THIS CODE, IT COULD BE CONTAINED IN PAPER-TAPE DATA, IN WHICH CASE
/	     IT WILL BE TREATED AS A LOWER-CASE CHARACTER TRANSLATED TO "^" [WHICH IS
/	     KNOWN AS EITHER <CARET> OR <UP-ARROW>] DEPENDING ON SPECIFIC TERMINAL
/	     CHARACTERISTICS.

/	12)  CODE 177 <RO> IS IGNORED; END-OF-LINE CONSIDERATIONS ARE NOT AFFECTED.

	TAD	(-177)			/COMPARE LATEST TO <RO> CODE.
	SNA				/SKIP IF NOT <RO>.
	JMP	IGNORE			/IGNORE <RO>; COULD BE BETWEEN <CR> AND <LF>.
	TAD	[-140+177]		/COMPARE TO LOWER-CASE LIMIT.
	SPA				/SKIP IF LOWER-CASE CHARACTER.
	TAD	[40]			/ELSE RESTORE IF UPPER-CASE CHARACTER.
	SNA				/IS IT <AT-SIGN> OR <ACCENT-MARK>?
	JMP	TOSSIT			/YES, THROW AWAY.
	TAD	(-"Z!300+100)		/COMPARE TO <^Z> [ALSO TIME-OUT VALUE].
	SNA				/SKIP IF OTHER.
	JMP	PTEOF			/JUMP IF <EOF> CHARACTER.
	TAD	(-"I+"Z)		/COMPARE TO <HT>.
	SNA				/SKIP OF ANY OTHER.
	TAD	(37-"I+300+200)		/KLUDGE TO CONVERT <HT> TO CODE 37.
	TAD	(-"M+"I)		/COMPARE TO <CR>.
	SNA				/SKIP IF ANY OTHER.
	JMP	OUTCR			/JUMP IF <CR>.
	IAC	/TAD	(-"L+"M)	/COMPARE TO <FF>.
	SNA				/SKIP IF ANY OTHER.
	JMP	OUTFF			/JUMP IF <FF>.
	TAD	[-"J+"L]		/COMPARE TO <LF>.
	SNA				/SKIP IF ANY OTHER.
	JMP	OUTLF			/JUMP IF <LF>.
	TAD	(-137+"J-300)		/IS IT <BACK-ARROW>?
	SNA				/SKIP IF ANY OTHER.
	JMP	TOSSIT			/THROW AWAY <BACK-ARROW>.
	TAD	[-40+137]		/COMPARE TO OTHER CONTROL CHARACTERS.
	SPA				/SKIP IF NOT A CONTROL CHARACTER [OR <NUL>].
	JMP	IGNORE			/IGNORE IN CASE JUNK CHAR BETWEEN <CR> AND <LF>.
	TAD	[40]			/RESTORE SIX-BIT CHARACTER.
	AND	[77]			/JUST SIX BITS.
	SKP				/DON'T DO <FF> OUTPUT.
/	COMES HERE TO OUTPUT THE SPECIAL <FF> INDICATOR CODE.

OUTFF,	NL2000				/SET <FF> INDICATOR VALUE.
OUTCR,	DCA	OUTCHAR			/SAVE FOR NOW.
	TAD	OUTCHAR			/GET THE CHARACTER.
	JMS I	(PQ6BIT)		/PUT INTO THE OUTPUT FILE.
	TAD	OUTCHAR			/GET IT BACK
	JMS I	(PSXBIT)		/PRINT THE CHARACTER.
TOSSIT,	TAD	PTLATEST		/GET THE LATEST CHARACTER.
	DCA	PTPREVIOUS		/SAVE AS PREVIOUS CHARACTER FOR NEXT TIME.
IGNORE,	CLA				/CLEAN UP [IN CASE IGNORING THE CHARACTER].
	JMP	RDRLOOP			/GO GET ANOTHER CHARACTER.

/	COMES HERE IF THE LATEST CHARACTER IS A <LF>.  IF THE PREVIOUS CHARACTER IS
/	<CR>, THEN IGNORE THE <LF> [BECAUSE <EOL> HAS ALREADY BEEN OUTPUT]; IF THE
/	PREVIOUS CHARACTER IS OTHER THAN <CR>, OUTPUT <EOL> NOW.

OUTLF,	TAD	PTPREVIOUS		/GET THE PREVIOUS CHARACTER.
	TAD	(-"M!300)		/COMPARE TO <CR>.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF OTHER THAN <CR>.
	JMP	TOSSIT			/IGNORE <LF> AFTER <CR>.

/	THE PREVIOUS CHARACTER WAS NOT <CR>; OUTPUT <EOL> NOW TO END THE LINE.  NEXT
/	TIME THE PREVIOUS CHARACTER WILL BE <LF> WHICH IS NOT <CR>.  THIS ALLOWS
/	STRING SEQUENCES SUCH AS SOME QUANTITY OF <LF> CHARACTERS TO CREATE AN
/	EQUIVALENT QUANTITY OF NULL-LENGTH LINES.  BECAUSE P?S/8 TEXT FILES SUPPORT
/	THE <EOL> AND NOT EITHER <CR> OR <LF> AS AN INDEPENDENT COMPONENT, THIS IS THE
/	BEST CONVERSION POSSIBLE.  FOR MOST LANGUAGES [SUCH AS PAL] THE OUTPUT
/	INTERPRETATION WILL BE AS ORIGINALLY INTENDED.

	JMP	OUTCR			/CONTINUE THERE TO OUTPUT <EOL>.

/	COMES HERE IF NO FURTHER PAPER-TAPE INPUT.

PTEOF,	CLA				/CLEAN UP.
	TAD	OUTCHAR			/GET LAST CHARACTER PLACED INTO THE OUTPUT FILE.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF IT WAS NOT <EOL>.
	JMP	CHECKMULTIPLE		/<EOL> WAS OUTPUT; GO CHECK FOR MULTIPLE TAPES.
	JMS I	(PSXBIT)		/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.
	JMS I	(PQ6BIT)		/OUTPUT <EOL> INTO THE FILE.

/	CHECK FOR /M [MULTIPLE INPUT PAPER-TAPES] HERE.

CHECKMU,JMP	CLSFILE			/**** /M OPTION SWITCH SET **** AND 0 [0000].

/	DO STUFF FOR SECONDARY INPUT TAPES IF /M HERE.

	NL0001				/SET THE INITIAL LINES COUNT
	DCA	LINCNT			/TO PRINT FOUR OPENING LINES.

/	ZBLOCK	3

	JMP	MORETAPES		/GO TO ANOTHER PAPER-TAPE THERE.
/	CHECK IF THERE WAS ANY PAPER-TAPE INPUT.

CLSFILE,TAD	TCNTLOW			/GET LOW-ORDER TOTAL FRAME COUNT.
	SNA				/SKIP IF SOME.
	TAD	TCNTHIGH		/GET HIGH-ORDER TOTAL FRAME COUNT.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF SOME INPUT.
	JMP I	(FNLRPT)		/PRODUCE FINAL REPORT ONLY IF NONE.
	JMS I	(PQCLOSE)		/CLOSE THE LATEST FILE.
	NL4000				/SET PAGE CLOSE VALUE.
	JMS I	(PSXBIT)		/FINISH THE LAST PAGE, BUT DON'T START ANOTHER.
/	JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.
	JMP I	(FNLRPT)		/PRODUCE FINAL REPORT AND EXIT THERE.

/	ROUTINE TO GET A CHARACTER FROM THE HIGH [OR LOW] SPEED READER.

/	CALL WITH:

/	JMS	RDRGET			/CALL ROUTINE.
/	END-OF-INPUT			/COMES HERE IF NO INPUT AVAILABLE [CONTROL-Z].
/	GOT-A-CHARACTER			/SKIP RETURN IF NOT CONTROL-Z.

RDRGET,	.-.				/GET A CHARACTER FROM THE PAPER-TAPE DEVICE.
	JMS I	RDRHANDLER		/CALL THE HIGH [OR LOW] SPEED READER HANDLER.
	DCA	INTEMP			/SAVE THE LATEST CHARACTER.
	TAD	INTEMP			/GET IT BACK.
	AND	[177]			/JUST ASCII BITS.
	TAD	(-"Z!300)		/COMPARE TO CONTROL-Z.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF OTHER THAN CONTROL-Z.
	JMP I	RDRGET			/TAKE IMMEDIATE RETURN IF NO [FURTHER] INPUT.
	ISZ	RDRGET			/BUMP PAST END-OF-INPUT ADDRESS.
	TAD	INTEMP			/GET THE LATEST CHARACTER BACK.
	JMP I	RDRGET			/SKIP RETURN TO CALLER.

RDRHAND,HIREAD				/DEVICE-SPECIFIC READER ROUTINE POINTER.
RDRINIT,HINIT				/DEVICE-SPECIFIC READER INITIALIZE ROUTINE.

	PAGE				/DUMP LITERALS NOW.

/	COMES HERE TO PRODUCE THE FINAL REPORT AND THEN EXIT.

/	DO FINAL REPORT STUFF HERE.

FNLRPT,	TAD	TCNTLOW			/GET LOW-ORDER TOTAL FRAME COUNT.
	SNA				/SKIP IF SOME.
	TAD	TCNTHIGH		/GET HIGH-ORDER TOTAL FRAME COUNT.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF THERE WERE NO DATA FRAMES.
	JMP	PSTNOMESSAGE		/JUMP PAST IF THERE WAS SOME INPUT.
	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/COMPLAIN OF
	INEOFMESSAGE			/NO INPUT.

/	REPORT THE PROCESSED FRAME COUNT [EITHER WAY].

PSTNOME,JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.

/	CHECK FOR EXACTLY ONE FRAME; IF SO, CHANGE THE MESSAGE.

	TAD	TCNTHIGH		/GET HIGH-ORDER HALF.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF ZERO.
	JMP	PRTPLURAL		/PRINT PLURAL IF LARGE NON-ZERO.
	NL7777				/SET -1.
	TAD	TCNTLOW			/CHECK IF LOW-ORDER IS EXACTLY 0001.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF SO.
PRTPLUR,TAD	("S^100)		/PUT THE PLURAL FORM IN THE MESSAGE.
	DCA I	(FRMSMSG+4)		/STORE EITHER WAY. 
	JMS I	(DPRINT)		/CALL DOUBLE-PRECISION PRINT ROUTINE.
	TCNTLOW				/POINTER TO LOW-ORDER HALF OF ARGUMENT.
	JMS I	(SCRIBE)		/CALL MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE
	FRMSMSG				/TO PRINT FRAME[S] MESSAGE.
	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/CALL MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE.
	RDMSG				/TO PRINT READ MESSAGE.
	JMP I	[SBOOT]			/EXIT TO P?S/8.

/	HIGH-SPEED READER INITIALIZE ROUTINE.

HINIT,	.-.				/HIGH-SPEED READER INITIALIZE ROUTINE.
	NL0001				/SET A NON-ZERO VALUE FOR
	DCA	RTIMER			/READER TIME-OUT COUNT.
	DCA	INFLAG			/INITIAL STATE - NO LEADER OR ANY OTHER FRAMES.
	DCA	INCNTLOW		/CLEAR LOW-ORDER FRAME COUNT FOR LATEST TAPE.
	DCA	INCNTHIGH		/CLEAR HIGH-ORDER FRAME COUNT FOR LATEST TAPE.

/	THERE MAY BE OTHER THINGS TO INITIALIZE HERE.

	JMP I	HINIT			/RETURN TO CALLER.
/	PRINT P?S/8 SIX-BIT TEXT PRINT ROUTINE.

/	CALL WITH:

/	ACCUMULATOR CONTAINS CODE TO PRINT.
/	JMS I	[PSXBIT]		/CALL THE P?S/8 SIX-BIT TEXT PRINT ROUTINE.

/	P?S/8 SIX-BIT CHARACTER CODES ARE CONVERTED AS FOLLOWS:

/	0000	PRINT <CR>/<LF>.

/	0037	PRINT <HT> USING <SP> CHARACTERS TO SIMULATE TABS; THIS IS IDENTICAL
/		TO THE CHARACTER PROCESSING OF HORIZONTAL TABS IN THE KEYBOARD MONITOR
/		WHEN THE 'TAB 3' COMMAND [OR EQUIVALENT] IS IN EFFECT.

/	01-36	PRINT CORRESPONDING P?S/8 SIXBIT TEXT CHARACTER.

/	40-77	PRINT CORRESPONDING P?S/8 SIXBIT TEXT CHARACTER.

/	SIX-BIT CHARACTER CODES ARE CONVERTED ACCORDING TO THE SAME METHODS USED TO
/	PROCESS CHARACTERS CREATED BY THE TEXT DIRECTIVE AND SIMILAR MECHANISMS.

/	TWO ADDITIONAL SPECIAL FUNCTIONS ARE SUPPORTED [PASSED IN THE ACCUMULATOR]:

/	2000	PRINT <FF> CHARACTER AS DETERMINED BY THE DISPLAY MODE IN EFFECT [IF
/		ANY].

/	4000	PRINT THE REST OF THE FINAL PAGE.  THIS IS ALSO DETERMINED BY THE
/		PARTICULARS OF THE DISPLAY MODE IN EFFECT.

/	NOTE: THE EXACT FUNCTIONALITY OF THIS ROUTINE IS SUBJECT TO DYNAMIC
/	INITIALIZATION MODIFICATIONS MADE DEPENDING ON THE PRESENCE [OR ABSENCE] OF
/	THE '/D', '/P' AND '/N' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES.

PSXBIT,	.-.				/PRINT P?S/8 SIX-BIT CHARACTER ROUTINE.
	DCA	PSXTMP			/SAVE PASSED VALUE.
	TAD	PSXTMP			/GET IT BACK.
	SPA CLA				/SKIP IF NOT PAGE FINISH.
	JMP	PAGEND			/JUMP IF FINISHING THE LAST PRINTED PAGE.
	NL2000				/SET <FF> BIT MASK
	AND	PSXTMP			/JUST <FF> BIT.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF NOT <FF>.
	JMP	DOFF			/JUMP IF SET.
/	A PRINTING CHARACTER WAS PASSED [NOT A SPECIAL FUNCTION].

/	CHECK IF AN OPENING HEADER HAS ALREADY BEEN PRINTED.

	TAD	OUTHDFLAG		/GET INITIAL HEADER FLAG.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF ALREADY OUTPUT.
	JMS I	(PGHEADERPRINT)		/PRINT OUT THE INITIAL HEADER.

/	CHECK IF AT THE LEFT MARGIN.  [ESSENTIALLY, THIS TEST IS EXCESSIVE.]

	TAD	COLUMN			/CHECK IF AT THE LEFT MARGIN.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF SO.
	JMP	PDOIT			/JUMP IF NOT.

/	THE PREVIOUS PAGE MIGHT HAVE BEEN THE FULL LENGTH ALLOWED [55 LINES].  IF SO,
/	A NEW HEADER IS REQUIRED.

	TAD	LINCNT			/GET THE CURRENT LINE COUNT.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF PREVIOUS PAGE WAS NOT A FULL PAGE.
	JMS I	(PGHEADERPRINT)		/PRINT OUT THE COMPLETE HEADER FIRST.
PDOIT,	TAD	PSXTMP			/GET PASSED VALUE AGAIN.
	SNA				/SKIP IF NOT <EOL> VALUE.
	JMP	DOCR			/JUMP IF IT IS <EOL>.
	TAD	[-37]			/COMPARE TO <HT> CODE VALUE.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF OTHERWISE.
	JMP	DOTAB			/JUMP IF <HT>.
	TAD	PSXTMP			/GET IT AGAIN
	JMS I	[P6CH]			/PRINT IT CONVERTED TO SEVEN-BIT FORM.
PSBXIT,	NL0001				/SET THE FLAG TO PREVENT
	DCA	OUTHDFLAG		/FURTHER INITIAL HEADERS.
	JMP I	 PSXBIT			/RETURN TO CALLER.

DOCR,	JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF> [CLEARS COLUMN COUNT].
	JMP	PSBXIT			/EXIT TO CALLER THERE.

/	COMES HERE TO HANDLE <HT> CODE.

DOTAB,	TAD	[" &77]			/GET A SPACE CHARACTER.
	JMS I	[P6CH]			/PRINT IT.
	TAD	COLUMN			/GET CURRENT COLUMN COUNT.
	AND	[7]			/JUST RELATIVE TAB BITS.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF AT THE BEGINNING OF THE NEXT TAB STOP.
	JMP	DOTAB			/GO DO ANOTHER IF NOT.
	JMP	PSBXIT			/EXIT TO CALLER THERE.

/	COMES HERE TO HANDLE <FF> CODE.

DOFF,	JMS I	(PGHEADERPRINT)		/PRINT OUT THE COMPLETE HEADER.
	JMP	PSBXIT			/EXIT TO CALLER THERE.

/	COMES HERE IF THE LAST PRINTED PAGE SHOULD BE FINISHED.

PAGEND,	NL7777				/INDICATE NO NEW HEADER.
	JMS I	(PGHEADERPRINT)		/PRINT OUT THE REST OF THE PAGE ONLY.
	JMP	PSBXIT			/EXIT TO CALLER THERE.
/	PRINT SIXBIT TEXT ROUTINE.

P6CH,	.-.				/SIX-BIT TEXT PRINT ROUTINE.
	TAD	[" &77]			/INVERT IT.
	AND	[77]			/JUST SIX-BIT.
	TAD	[" &77]			/NOW HAVE SEVEN-BIT.
	JMS I	[P7CH]			/GO PRINT IT.
	ISZ	COLUMN			/BUMP COLUMN COUNTER.
	NOP				/JUST IN CASE!
	JMP I	P6CH			/RETURN TO CALLER.

PRCRLFS,.-.				/PRINT MULTIPLE <CR>/<LF> ROUTINE.
	JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.
	TAD	LINCNT			/GET LINE COUNTER.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF IT OVERFLOWED.
	JMP	.-3			/JUMP IF NOT.
	JMP I	PRCRLFS			/RETURN.

PQ6BIT,	.-.				/OUTPUT SIX-BIT CHARACTER INTO P?S/8 FILE.

/	PROCESS STUFF HERE.

	CLA				/CLEAN UP.
	JMP I	PQ6BIT			/RETURN TO CALLER.

/	P?S/8 FILE INITIALIZE ROUTINE.

PQINITI,.-.				/P?S/8 FILE INITIALIZE ROUTINE.

/	PERFORM OTHER FILE-ORIENTED INITIALIZE STUFF HERE.

/	ADDITIONAL INITIALIZATION STUFF.

	TAD	["J&37]			/GET <LF> CODE.
	DCA	PTPREVIOUS		/INITIALIZE PREVIOUS CHARACTER PROCESSED.
	NL0001				/SET THE INITIAL LINES COUNT
	DCA	LINCNT			/TO PRINT FOUR OPENING LINES.
	DCA	OUTHDFLAG		/PRINT HEADER BEFORE ANY INPUT.
	DCA	OUTCHAR			/NO INPUT YET.

/	TAD	(-LINES)		/SETUP THE LINE
/	DCA	LINCNT			/COUNT [PER PAGE].
	JMP I	PQINITIALIZE		/RETURN TO CALLER.

PQCLOSE,.-.				/P?S/8 FILE CLOSE ROUTINE.
	JMP I	PQCLOSE			/RETURN TO CALLER.

	PAGE				/DUMP LITERALS NOW.
/	SUPPORT ROUTINES.

/	CONSOLE OUTPUT ROUTINE; DO NOT USE FOR PAPER-TAPE OUTPUT.

/	PRINT SEVEN-BIT CONSOLE OUTPUT ROUTINE.

/	SUPPORTS CONTROL-S/CONTROL-Q PROTOCOL.

/	SUPPORTS CONTROL-O TO FLIP OUTPUT OFF AND ON [WHILE DEFINITELY OUTPUTTING "^O"
/	EVERY TIME CONTROL-O IS HIT].

/	SUPPORTS SETTING THE LOGICAL ABORT SWITCH FOR TOTAL COMPATIBILITY WITH ALL
/	MODELS INCLUDING DECMATES.

/	ALLOWS MODIFICATION FOR FULL COMPATIBILITY WITH THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY.

/	DOES NOT SUPPORT MODIFICATION FOR THE LINE PRINTER [WHICH WOULD ALSO AFFECT
/	THE SUPPORT FOR THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY] BECAUSE THE PROGRAM DOESN'T
/	REQUIRE THIS FEATURE.

/	PRINTS THE SEVEN-BIT ASCII CHARACTER PASSED IN AC[5-11].

/	RETURNS WITH CLEAR AC.

P7CH,	.-.				/PRINT SEVEN-BIT CHARACTERS ON THE CONSOLE.
	DCA	P7TEMP			/SAVE PASSED VALUE FOR LATER.
P7AGAIN,JMS	CHKCONTROL		/CHECK FOR <^O>, <^C>, <^S>, <^Q> ETC.
	TAD	P7ECHO			/GET ECHO SWITCH.
	SPA CLA				/SKIP IF ECHO CURRENTLY ON.
	JMP	P7ECOFF			/JUMP IF OUTPUT DISABLED BY <^O>.
	TAD	P7TEMP			/GET THE PASSED VALUE BACK.
P7TSF,	TSF+DEBUGOFFSET			/OUTPUT FLAG UP?
P7JMP,	JMP	P7AGAIN			/NO, GO CHECK FOR CONTROL CHARACTERS.
P7TLS,	TLS+DEBUGOFFSET			/YES OUTPUT THE CHARACTER.

/	IF THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS IN EFFECT, THE THREE INSTRUCTIONS ABOVE WILL
/	BE CHANGED TO THE FOLLOWING:

	NOPUNCH				/FOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

	*P7TSF				/BACKUP THREE WORDS.

	CIF	/MCS+10			/WILL BE "CIF MCS+10" [TO OVERLAY FIELD].
	JMS	OUTCON			/CALL CONSOLE OUTPUT ROUTINES.
	JMP	P7AGAIN			/NOT DONE YET, GO CHECK FOR CONTROL CHARACTERS.

	ENPUNCH				/UN-FOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

/	COMES DIRECTLY HERE IF ECHO IS OFF.

P7ECOFF,JMS	CHKCONTROL		/CHECK FOR <^O>, <^C>, <^S>, <^Q> ETC.
/	CLA				/CLEAN UP [NOT NEEDED].
	JMP I	P7CH			/RETURN TO CALLER.
/	CHECK FOR CONTROL-O ROUTINE.

/	PRINTS "^O" IF CONTROL-O IS PRESSED AND REVERSES CHARACTER PRINTING MODE.

/	ALSO CHECKS FOR <^C>, <^S>, <^Q> ETC.

/	CONLATEST WILL CONTAIN THE LATEST [NON-CONTROL] CHARACTER [IF ANY].

CHKCONT,.-.				/CHECK FOR CONTROL-O.
	JMS	CTLCTST			/CHECK FOR <^C>, <^S>, <^Q>.
	TAD	(-"O!300)		/NOT ANY OF THEM; COMPARE TO <^O>.
	SNA				/SKIP IF NOT <^O>.
	JMP	OUTO			/GO HANDLE <^O> THERE.
	TAD	(-"S+"O)		/COMPARE TO <^S>.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF A MATCH.
	JMP I	CHKCONTROL		/RETURN ON NON-MATCH.

/	CONTROL-S FOUND; MUST GET CONTROL-Q BEFORE RETURNING TO HONOR THE PROTOCOL.

CNTQLUP,JMS	CTLCTST			/CHECK FOR <^C>, <^S>, <^Q>.
	TAD	[-"Q!300]		/COMPARE TO <^Q>.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF A MATCH.
	JMP	CNTQLUP			/GO BACK IF NOT.
	DCA	CONLATEST		/CLEAR THE INPUT BUFFER.
	JMP I	CHKCONTROL		/CONTROL-Q DETECTED; WE CAN RETURN NOW.

/	COMES HERE IF CONTROL-O WAS PRESSED.

OUTO,	TAD	("^&177)		/GET "^" CHARACTER.
	JMS	P7OUT			/DISPLAY IT.
	TAD	("O&177)		/GET "O" CHARACTER.
	JMS	P7OUT			/DISPLAY IT.
	NL4000				/SET AC[0].
	TAD	P7ECHO			/FLIP ECHO SWITCH.
	DCA	P7ECHO			/STORE BACK.
	DCA	CONLATEST		/CLEAR INPUT BUFFER.
	JMP I	CHKCONTROL		/RETURN TO CALLER.

/	PRINT <CR>/<LF> ROUTINE.

CRLF,	.-.				/PRINT <CR>, <LF> ROUTINE.
	CLA				/CLEAN UP JUST IN CASE.
	TAD	["M&37]			/GET A <CR>.
	JMS	P7CH			/PRINT IT.
	TAD	["J&37]			/GET A <LF>.
	JMS	P7CH			/PRINT IT.
	DCA	COLUMN			/NOW AT LEFT MARGIN.
	ISZ	LINCNT			/BUMP LINE COUNTER.
	NOP				/IN CASE IT SKIPS.
	JMP I	CRLF			/RETURN.
/	ROUTINE TO CHECK FOR CONTROL CHARACTERS WHILE WAITING FOR THE OUTPUT FLAG.

CTLCTST,.-.				/CHECK FOR <^C>, <^S>, <^Q>.
	CLA				/CLEAN UP.
	DCA	CONLATEST		/CLEAR INPUT BUFFER.
CHKKSF,	KSF				/KEYBOARD FLAG UP?
CHKJMP,	JMP I	CTLCTST			/NO, JUST RETURN.
CHKKRS,	KRS/KRB				/YES, READ KEYBOARD PRESERVING THE FLAG.
					/NOTE: CHANGED TO "KRB" ON DECMATES.

/	IF THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS IN EFFECT, THE THREE INSTRUCTIONS ABOVE WILL
/	BE CHANGED TO THE FOLLOWING:

	NOPUNCH				/FOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

	*CHKKSF				/BACKUP THREE WORDS.

	CIF	/MCS+10			/WILL BE "CIF MCS+10" [TO OVERLAY FIELD].
	JMS	INCON			/CALL CONSOLE INPUT ROUTINES.
	JMP I	CTLCTST			/RETURN IF NO KEYBOARD INPUT.

	ENPUNCH				/UN-FOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

	AND	[177]			/REMOVE PARITY BIT.
	DCA	CONLATEST		/SAVE FOR NOW.
	NL7775				/SET AC TO -3.
	TAD	CONLATEST		/COMPARE TO LATEST KEYBOARD CHARACTER.
	SNA				/SKIP IF NOT <^C>.
	ISZ I	(SCRSIZE)		/SET LOGICAL ABORT IF <^C> PRESSED.
	SPA SNA CLA			/SKIP IF GREATER THAN <^C>.
	JMP I	[SBOOT]			/ABORT ON <BRK>, <^A>, <^B> OR <^C>.
CHKKCC,	KCC				/CLEAR FLAG NOW.

	NOPUNCH				/FOOL THE ASSEMBLER

	*CHKKCC				/BACKUP ONE WORD.

	AND	0			/DON'T USE THE "KCC" INSTRUCTION IF THE
					/LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS ENABLED OR IF
					/RUNNING ON A DECMATE-BASED SYSTEM.

	ENPUNCH				/UNFOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

	TAD	CONLATEST		/GET THE CHARACTER BACK.
	JMP I	CTLCTST			/RETURN TO CALLER.
/	STRING MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE [SCRIBE].

/	CALLING SEQUENCE:

/	JMS I	(SCRIBE)		/CALL MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE.
/	MESSADR				/MESSAGE ADDRESS POINTER.
/	RETURNS HERE			/RETURNS PAST THE MESSAGE ADDRESS POINTER.

/	THE AC IS IGNORED WHEN CALLED; ROUTINE EXITS WITH CLEAR AC.

/	MESSAGE FORMAT.

/	SIX-BIT TEXT WITH ENHANCEMENTS:

/  1)	00 - END OF MESSAGE.

/  2)	36 - ^ MEANS FLIP UPPER-CASE/LOWER-CASE.

/  3)	45 - % MEANS PRINT <CR>/<LF>.

/	ALL OTHER SIX-BIT CHARACTERS HAVE THEIR USUAL MEANING.  ALPHABETIC CHARACTERS
/	WILL BE PRINTED IN THE CASE CHOSEN [UNLESS THE /U OPTION SWITCH IS SET WHICH
/	FORCES UPPER-CASE OUTPUT].


SCRIBE,	.-.				/MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE.
	CLA				/CLEAN UP JUST IN CASE.
	TAD I	SCRIBE			/GET MESSAGE POINTER.
	DCA	SCRPTR			/STASH IT.
	ISZ	SCRIBE			/BUMP PAST MESSAGE POINTER ARGUMENT.
	TAD	(140)			/SETUP FOR LOWER-CASE DEFAULT.
CASZP1,	DCA	SCRCASE			/SETUP INITIAL CASE.

/	IF THE /U OPTION SWITCH IS SET, THE PREVIOUS INSTRUCTION WILL BE CHANGED TO
/	THE FOLLOWING:

	NOPUNCH				/FOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

	*CASZP1				/BACKUP ONE WORD.

	CLA!400				/THROW AWAY LOWER-CASE DEFAULT.

	ENPUNCH				/UNFOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

/	THIS IS THE BASIC CHARACTER UNPACKING ROUTINE.

SCRLUP,	TAD I	SCRPTR			/GET LEFT HALF-WORD.
	RTR;RTR;RTR			/MOVE DOWN TO RIGHT HALF OF THE AC.
	JMS	SCRPRNT			/PRINT IT.
	TAD I	SCRPTR			/GET RIGHT HALF-WORD.
	JMS	SCRPRNT			/PRINT IT.
	ISZ	SCRPTR			/BUMP POINTER TO NEXT PAIR.
	JMP	SCRLUP			/KEEP GOING.
SCRPRNT,.-.				/SIX-BIT CHARACTER PRINT ROUTINE.
	AND	[77]			/JUST RIGHT HALF SIX-BIT CHARACTER BITS.
	SNA				/END OF MESSAGE?
	JMP I	SCRIBE			/YES, RETURN TO OVERALL CALLER.
	DCA	SCRCHAR			/NO, SAVE IT FOR NOW.
	TAD	SCRCHAR			/GET THE CHARACTER BACK.
	TAD	(-"%!200)		/IS IT "%"?
	SNA				/SKIP IF NOT.
	JMP	SCRCRLF			/JUMP IF IT MATCHES.
	TAD	[-"^+100+"%]		/IS IT "^"?
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF NOT.
	JMP	SCRFLIP			/JUMP IF IT MATCHES.

/	NOT A SPECIAL CHARACTER.

	TAD	SCRCHAR			/GET THE CHARACTER.
	AND	[40]			/DOES CASE MATTER?
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF NOT.
	TAD	SCRCASE			/ELSE GET PREVAILING CASE.
	TAD	SCRCHAR			/ADD ON CHARACTER.
	JMS	P7CH			/PRINT THE CHARACTER [POSSIBLY CORRECTED].
	JMP I	SCRPRNT			/RETURN TO OUR CALLER.

/	COMES HERE IF THE LATEST CHARACTER IS "%".

SCRCRLF,JMS I	[CRLF]			/DO A <CR>, <LF>.
	JMP I	SCRPRNT			/RETURN TO OUR CALLER.

/	COMES HERE IF THE LATEST CHARACTER IS "^".

SCRFLIP,TAD	SCRCASE			/GET CURRENT CASE VALUE.
	CIA				/INVERT IT.
	TAD	(140+100)		/ADD SUM OF POSSIBLE VALUES.
CASZP2,	DCA	SCRCASE			/SAVE NOW FLIPPED CASE VALUE.

/	IF THE /U OPTION SWITCH IS SET, THE PREVIOUS INSTRUCTION WILL BE CHANGED TO
/	THE FOLLOWING:

	NOPUNCH				/FOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

	*CASZP2				/BACKUP ONE WORD.

	CLA!400				/THROW AWAY LOWER-CASE DEFAULT.

	ENPUNCH				/UNFOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

	JMP I	SCRPRNT			/RETURN TO OUR CALLER.
/	DEDICATED SEVEN-BIT OUTPUT ROUTINE FOR USE ONLY WITH CONTROL-O ROUTINE.

P7OUT,	.-.				/DEDICATED SEVEN-BIT PRINT ROUTINE.
P7OCHK,	TSF+DEBUGOFFSET			/FLAG UP?
P7OJMP,	JMP	P7OCHK			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
P7OTLS,	TLS+DEBUGOFFSET			/YES, PRINT THE CHARACTER.

/	IF THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS IN EFFECT, THE THREE INSTRUCTIONS ABOVE WILL
/	BE CHANGED TO THE FOLLOWING:

	NOPUNCH				/FOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

	*P7OCHK				/BACKUP THREE WORDS.

	CIF	/MCS+10			/WILL BE "CIF MCS+10" [TO OVERLAY FIELD].
	JMS	OUTCON			/CALL CONSOLE OUTPUT ROUTINES.
	JMP	P7OCHK			/NOT DONE YET, WAIT FOR IT.

	ENPUNCH				/UN-FOOL THE ASSEMBLER.

	CLA				/CLEAN UP.
	JMP I	P7OUT			/RETURN TO CALLER.

P7ECHO,	0				/OUTPUT ECHO STATUS; INITIALIZED FOR ECHO ON.
P7TEMP,	.-.				/PASSED OUTPUT CHARACTER.
SCRCASE,100				/ALPHABETIC CASE; INITIALIZED FOR UPPER-CASE.
SCRCHAR,.-.				/SCRIBE LATEST OUTPUT CHARACTER.
SCRPTR,	.-.				/SCRIBE MESSAGE POINTER.

	PAGE				/DUMP LITERALS NOW.
/	LOW-SPEED READER [ASR TELETYPE] INPUT ROUTINE.

/	THIS IS THE INPUT ROUTINE USED TO READ PAPER-TAPE INPUT ON THE LOW-SPEED
/	READER OF A TELETYPE MODEL 33 ASR OR MODEL 35 ASR TELETYPE.  DUE TO HARDWARE
/	CONSTRAINTS, CERTAIN CONTROL FUNCTIONS ARE NOT SUPPORTED [INCLUDING THE
/	LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY]; THE KEYBOARD MUST NOT BE PRESSED WHILE THE READER
/	STATION IS PROVIDING PAPER-TAPE INPUT.

/	ALL INPUT IS SUBJECT TO TIME-OUT.  WHEN THE READER IS ENABLED, CHARACTERS
/	SHOULD BE AVAILABLE EVERY TENTH OF A SECOND UNTIL THE READER RUNS OUT OF
/	PAPER-TAPE [OR THE PAPER-TAPE TANGLES].  FAILING TO OBTAIN A CHARACTER WITHIN
/	A SECOND OR TWO WILL LOGICALLY CLOSE THE DEVICE BY RETURNING THE CONTROL-Z
/	CHARACTER.  [NOTE: THE PAPER-TAPE INPUT CAN SELF-CLOSE IF A CONTROL-Z IS
/	PRESENT ON THE PAPER-TAPE, GENERALLY AFTER THE LAST TRAILER FRAME.]

/	IF THE MULTIPLE INPUT TAPE MODE ['/M' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS SET] IS IN
/	EFFECT AND MULTIPLE INPUT TAPES ARE BEING PROCESSED, EVENTUALLY THE LATEST
/	OPEN FILE WILL BE CLOSED ON CONTROL-Z DETECTION; FINAL REPORTS ON FILE
/	CREATION ARE MADE JUST PRIOR TO PROGRAM EXIT.  WHILE THE PROGRAM IS WAITING
/	FOR CONFIRMATION OF THE NEXT INPUT TAPE, CONTROL CHARACTERS CAN BE CHECKED
/	THAT CAN LEAD TO PROGRAM ABORT OR ECHO STATUS REVERSAL, ETC.

LOWREAD,.-.				/LOW-SPEED INPUT ROUTINE.
	CLA				/CLEAN UP
	DCA	LINNER			/CLEAR INNER LOOP COUNTER.
	TAD	(-OUTIME)		/SETUP
	DCA	LOUTER			/OUTER LOOP COUNTER.
LRLOOP,	KSF				/KEYBOARD FLAG UP?
	JMP	LRTIM1			/NO, KEEP WAITING.
	KRB				/YES, READ IN THE CHARACTER.
	AND	[177]			/JUST SEVEN-BIT ASCII.
	JMP I	LOWREAD			/RETURN TO CALLER.

/	COMES HERE IF NO DATA YET.

LRTIM1,	ISZ	LINNER			/WAITED ENOUGH?
	JMP	LRLOOP			/NO, KEEP GOING
	ISZ	LOUTER			/WAITED TOO MUCH?
	JMP	LRLOOP			/NO, KEEP GOING.

/	WE'VE WAITED ENOUGH.  NO MORE PAPER-TAPE INPUT.

	TAD	["Z&37]			/GET CONTROL-Z CODE

	*.-1				/FOR LOW-SPEED DEBUGGING.

	JMP	LRLOOP			/PREVENT TIME-OUT.

	JMP I	LOWREAD			/RETURN TO CALLER.

LINNER,	.-.				/INNER TIME-OUT COUNTER.
LOUTER,	.-.				/OUTER TIME-OUT COUNTER.
/	DOUBLE-PRECISION [UP TO EIGHT DIGITS] PRINT ROUTINE.

/	CALL WITH:

/	JMS I	(DPRINT)		/CALL DOUBLE-PRECISION PRINT ROUTINE.
/	DPARG				/POINTER TO LOW-ORDER HALF OF ARGUMENT.
/	RETURN				/RETURNS PAST IN-LINE ARGUMENT.

/	NOTE: THE PASSED DOUBLE-PRECISION ARGUMENT MUST BE IN THE RANGE OF 00,000,001
/	THROUGH 16,777,215 [ANY NON-ZERO UNSIGNED DOUBLE-PRECISION VALUE].

/	IF THE PASSED ARGUMENT IS 00,000,000, "NO" WILL PRINT ON THE SYSTEM CONSOLE.

DPRINT,	.-.				/DOUBLE-PRECISION PRINT ROUTINE.
	NL7777				/BACKUP DUE TO AUTO-INDEX.
	TAD I	DPRINT			/GET PASSED ARGUMENT.
	DCA	XR0			/STASH THE POINTER.
	TAD I	XR0			/GET THE LOW-ORDER HALF.
	DCA	DPACLOW			/STORE IN OUR ACCUMULATOR [LOW].
	TAD I	XR0			/GET THE HIGH-ORDER HALF.
	DCA	DPACHI			/STORE IN OUR ACCUMULATOR [HIGH].
	ISZ	DPRINT			/BUMP RETURN ADDRESS PAST IN-LINE ARGUMENT.
	TAD	[-10]			/SETUP THE LARGEST
	DCA	DIGCNT			/DIGIT COUNT.
	TAD	(DIGBUFFER+7+1)		/SETUP POINTER TO LOWEST DIGIT IN THE
	DCA	DIGPTR			/BUFFER.  [NOTE: WILL BE PRE-DECREMENTED.]
DPNEXT,	DCA	QUOLOW			/CLEAR LOW-ORDER QUOTIENT.
	DCA	QUOHI			/CLEAR HIGH-ORDER QUOTIENT.
DPLOOP,	CLL				/CLEAR LINK FOR DP ARITHMETIC PURPOSES.
	TAD	DPACLOW			/GET LOW-ORDER
	TAD	(7766)			/ADD LOW-ORDER HALF OF 7777,7766.
	DCA	DPACLOW			/STORE BACK.
	RAL				/GET CARRY BIT.
	TAD	DPACHI			/ADD ON HIGH-ORDER BIT.
	TAD	(7777)			/ADD HIGH-ORDER HALF OF 7777,7766.
	DCA	DPACHI			/STORE BACK.
	SNL				/SKIP IF NO UNDERFLOW YET.
	JMP	DPUNDER			/JUMP IF WE WENT TOO FAR.
	ISZ	QUOLOW			/BUMP LOW-ORDER QUOTIENT.
	SKP				/SKIP IF LOW-ORDER DID'T OVERFLOW.
	ISZ	QUOHI			/ELSE BUMP HIGH-ORDER QUOTIENT.
	JMP	DPLOOP			/KEEP GOING.

/	COMES HERE IF WE JUST WENT NEGATIVE.

DPUNDER,NL7777				/\
	TAD	DIGPTR			/ >BACKUP THE DIGIT POINTER.
	DCA	DIGPTR			//
	TAD	DPACLOW			/GET LOW-ORDER.
	TAD	[12]			/RESTORE TO 0-9.
	DCA I	DIGPTR			/STORE THE LATEST DIGIT [LOWEST FIRST]
	TAD	QUOLOW			/GET LOW-ORDER QUOTIENT.
	DCA	DPACLOW			/STORE AS LOW-ORDER DP ACCUMULATOR.
	TAD	QUOHI			/GET HIGH-ORDER QUOTIENT.
	DCA	DPACHI			/STORE AS HIGH-ORDER DP ACCUMULATOR.
	ISZ	DIGCNT			/DONE EIGHT DIGITS YET?
	JMP	DPNEXT			/NO, GO DO SOME MORE.

/	PROCESSED ALL EIGHT DIGITS; NOW PRINT THEM.

	TAD	(DIGBUFFER-1)		/SETUP THE
	DCA	XR0			/AUTO-INDEXED POINTER.
	TAD	[-10]			/SETUP THE
	DCA	DIGCNT			/DIGIT COUNTER.
	DCA	DIGFLG			/CLEAR DIGITS PRINTED FLAG.
DPRLUP,	TAD I	XR0			/GET A DIGIT
	SZA				/SKIP IF A ZERO.
	JMP	DPOUT			/OUTPUT ANY NON-ZERO DIGIT.
	TAD	DIGFLG			/PRINTED ANY YET?
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF SO.
	JMP	DPNOPRT			/IGNORE LEADING ZEROES.
DPOUT,	TAD	("0&177)		/MAKE IT ASCII.
	JMS I	(P7CH)			/PRINT IT.
	ISZ	DIGFLG			/INDICATE AT LEAST ONE DIGIT ALREADY PRINTED.
DPNOPRT,ISZ	DIGCNT			/DONE ALL DIGITS?
	JMP	DPRLUP			/NO, KEEP GOING.
	TAD	DIGFLG			/DID WE PRINT ANYTHING?
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF NOT.
	JMP I	DPRINT			/YES, RETURN TO CALLER.
	JMS I	(SCRIBE)		/CALL MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE.
	NOMSG				/PRINT NO MESSAGE.
	JMP I	DPRINT			/RETURN TO CALLER.

DIGBUFF,ZBLOCK 10			/DIGIT BUFFER.
DIGCNT,	.-.				/DIGIT COUNTER.
DIGFLG,	0				/DIGIT PRINTED FLAG; 1=PRINT LEADING ZEROES.
DIGPTR,	.-.				/DIGIT POINTER.
DPACLO,	.-.				/LOW-ORDER DOUBLE-PRECISION ACCUMULATOR.
DPACHI,	.-.				/HIGH-ORDER DOUBLE-PRECISION ACCUMULATOR.
QUOLOW,	.-.				/LOW-ORDER DOUBLE-PRECISION QUOTIENT.
QUOHI,	.-.				/HIGH-ORDER DOUBLE-PRECISION QUOTIENT.
NOMSG,	TEXT	"^NO"			/NO MESSAGE FOR ZERO ARGUMENTS.

	PAGE				/DUMP LITERALS NOW.
/	P?S/8 TEXT PROCESSING OUTPUT ROUTINE.  [CALLED AS A SUBROUTINE FOR NOW.]

/	WITH THE EXCEPTION OF <FF> HANDLING, THIS ROUTINE CONVERTS SEVEN-BIT ASCII
/	TEXT CHARACTERS FROM THE PAPER-TAPE READ ROUTINES INTO THE P?S/8 SIX-BIT
/	CHARACTER SET [AND EVENTUALLY PROCESSES THE CONVERTED CHARACTER INTO THE
/	CURRENT P?S/8 OUTPUT FILE].

/	CHARACTER DISPOSITION:

/	<NUL>	THE READER ROUTINE HAS ALREADY FILTERED OUT <NUL> AND LEADER/TRAILER
/	FRAMES; THIS CASE CANNOT OCCUR.

/	<HT>	CONVERT TO P?S/8 INTERNAL CODE 37.

/	<LF>	IGNORED IF JUST AFTER A <CR>.  OUTPUT P?S/8 <EOL> IF NOT.

/	<CR>	OUTPUT P?S/8 <EOL>.

/	<FF>	CONVERT TO 2000 TO ALLOW DEFERRED <FF> HANDLING.

/	<^Z>	THE READER ROUTINE HAS ALREADY FILTERED OUT CONTROL-Z [OR PHYSICAL
/		READER TIME-OUT, WHICH ARE LOGICALLY INDISTINGUISHABLE].  THIS ROUTINE
/		WILL NOT BE CALLED IF THE PAPER-TAPE LOGICAL END CONDITION HAS BEEN
/		REACHED; EXTERNAL ROUTINES WILL DETERMINE THE NEXT ACTION [EITHER END
/		THE LATEST OUTPUT FILE OR PERHAPS OBTAIN ADDITIONAL PAPER-TAPE INPUT
/		IF THE MULTIPLE INPUT TAPE MODE ['/M' COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCH IS
/		SET] IS IN EFFECT.

/	ALL OTHER CONTROL CHARACTERS WILL BE ACKNOWLEDGED AND IGNORED.

/	<RO>	RUBOUT CHARACTERS WILL BE IGNORED [IN CASE <CR> <RO> <LF>.]

PQSOUT,	.-.				/P?S/8 TEXT PROCESSING OUTPUT ROUTINE.
	DCA	 PQTEMP			/SAVE PASSED VALUE.


	JMP I	PQSOUT			/RETURN TO CALLER.

PQTEMP,	.-.				/OUTPUT TEMPORARY.

	PAGE				/DUMP THE LITERALS NOW.
/	HIGH-SPEED READER INPUT ROUTINE.

/	THIS IS THE INPUT ROUTINE USED TO READ PAPER-TAPE INPUT FROM THE HIGH-SPEED
/	READER [PC04, ETC.].  FOR FULL COMPATIBILITY WITH ALL MODELS, A
/	DOUBLE-BUFFERED APPROACH IS USED.  [NOTE: THIS CAN BE DEFEATED FOR USE WITH
/	THE SIMH SIMULATOR OR OTHER SITUATIONS WHERE ALL CHARACTERS ARE VALID AND
/	SHOULD BE USED; THAT IS THE DEFAULT MODE UNLESS THE '/2' COMMAND-LINE OPTION
/	SWITCH IS SET TO ENABLE THIS DOUBLE-BUFFERED INPUT ROUTINE.]

/	ALL INPUT IS SUBJECT TO TIME-OUT.  WHEN THE READER IS ENABLED, CHARACTERS
/	SHOULD ARRIVE WITHIN A TENTH OF A SECOND UNTIL THE READER RUNS OUT OF
/	PAPER-TAPE [OR THE PAPER-TAPE TANGLES].  FAILING TO OBTAIN A CHARACTER WITHIN
/	THIS TIME PERIOD WILL LOGICALLY CLOSE THE DEVICE BY RETURNING THE CONTROL-Z
/	CHARACTER.  [NOTE: THE PAPER-TAPE INPUT CAN SELF-CLOSE IF A CONTROL-Z IS
/	PRESENT ON THE PAPER-TAPE, GENERALLY AFTER THE LAST TRAILER FRAME.]

/	"RTIMER" MUST BE SET TO A NON-ZERO VALUE [0001] TO [RE]OPEN THE READER; CALLING
/	THE HIGH-SPEED READER ROUTINE AFTER THE DEVICE TIMES OUT RETURNS CONTROL-Z.

HIREAD,	.-.				/HIGH-SPEED READER INPUT ROUTINE.
	CLA				/CLEANUP.
HIZAP,	JMP	HNOBUFFER		/**** /2 OPTION SWITCH SET **** AND 0 [0000].
	TAD	RTIMER			/CHECK IF ALREADY TIMED-OUT.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF READER ACTIVE.
	JMP	HOVER			/JUMP IF WE NEED TO CLEAR THE BUFFER.
	RFC				/STARTUP ANOTHER CHARACTER FROM THE READER.
	DCA	RTIMER			/INITIALIZE THE TIME-OUT COUNTER.
HWAIT,	ISZ	RTIMER			/WAITED TOO LONG?
	JMP	HWATLP			/NO, KEEP GOING.
HOVER,	TAD	["Z&37]			/YES, GET CONTROL-Z CHARACTER
	DCA	HBUFFER			/CLEAR BUFFER [OR PUT CONTROL-Z IN IT].
	JMP	HLEAVE			/CLEAR LAST FRAME VALUE AND LEAVE FOR NOW.

/	THE TIME-OUT LOOP IS ADJUSTED TO TAKE AROUND 100 MILLISECONDS GIVE OR TAKE
/	DEPENDING ON THE MACHINE MODEL.

HWATLP,	TAD	HLATEST			/GET THE LATEST CHARACTER FROM LAST TIME.
	DCA	HBUFFER			/STASH IT FOR EVENTUAL EXIT.

	ZBLOCK	3			/"AND 0" INSTRUCTIONS TO ADJUST LOOP TIME.

	RSF				/FLAG UP?
	JMP	HWAIT			/NO, GO BACK AND WAIT.
	RRB				/YES, CLEAR THE FLAG AND READ THE LATEST FRAME.
HLEAVE,	DCA	HLATEST			/SAVE IT [OR PERHAPS CLEAR IT].
	TAD	HBUFFER			/GET PREVIOUS FRAME.
	JMP I	HIREAD			/RETURN TO CALLER.
/	COMES HERE IF THE DOUBLE-BUFFERED READER INPUT IS DISABLED.

/	UNBUFFERED HIGH-SPEED READER INPUT ROUTINE.

/	ALL INPUT IS SUBJECT TO TIME-OUT.  WHEN THE READER IS ENABLED, CHARACTERS
/	SHOULD ARRIVE WITHIN A TENTH OF A SECOND UNTIL THE READER RUNS OUT OF
/	PAPER-TAPE [OR THE PAPER-TAPE TANGLES].  FAILING TO OBTAIN A CHARACTER WITHIN
/	THIS TIME PERIOD WILL LOGICALLY CLOSE THE DEVICE BY RETURNING THE CONTROL-Z
/	CHARACTER.  [NOTE: THE PAPER-TAPE INPUT CAN SELF-CLOSE IF A CONTROL-Z IS
/	PRESENT ON THE PAPER-TAPE, GENERALLY AFTER THE LAST TRAILER FRAME.]

HNOBUFF,RFC				/STARTUP ANOTHER CHARACTER FROM THE READER.
	DCA	RTIMER			/INITIALIZE THE TIME-OUT COUNTER.
HWAIT0,	ISZ	RTIMER			/WAITED TOO LONG?
	JMP	HWAT0LP			/NO, KEEP GOING.
	TAD	["Z&37]			/YES, GET CONTROL-Z CHARACTER.
	JMP I	HIREAD			/RETURN TO CALLER.

/	THE TIME-OUT LOOP IS ADJUSTED TO TAKE AROUND 100 MILLISECONDS GIVE OR TAKE
/	DEPENDING ON THE MACHINE MODEL.

HWAT0LP,ZBLOCK	5			/"AND 0" INSTRUCTIONS TO ADJUST LOOP TIME.

	RSF				/FLAG UP?
	JMP	HWAIT0			/NO, GO BACK AND WAIT.
	RRB				/YES, CLEAR THE FLAG AND READ THE LATEST FRAME.
	JMP I	HIREAD			/RETURN TO CALLER.

HBUFFER,.-.				/BUFFERED FRAME DATA.
HLATEST,.-.				/LATEST FRAME DATA.

DATMSG,	TEXT	" ^00-M^ON-^"		/TODAY'S DAY AND MONTH WILL BE FILLED IN.

	DAYNUM=	DATMSG+1		/WHERE TO PATCH NUMERICAL DAY OF THE MONTH.
	MONTXT=	DATMSG+2		/WHERE TO PATCH MONTH TEXT [THREE WORDS].

DAYBLB,	TEXT	"^W^EDNESDAY"		/WILL BE DAY OF THE WEEK MESSAGE.
HSRMSG,	TEXT	"^H^IGH-"		/HIGH MESSAGE.
LSRMSG,	TEXT	"^L^OW-^"		/LOW MESSAGE.
PAGMSG,	TEXT	"  ^P^AGE "		/PAGE MESSAGE.

/	MAIN BODY OF PAGE HEADER MESSAGE.

TTLMSG,	TEXT	"^S^PEED ^R^EADER ^I^NPUT  ^P?S/8^ "
PROGMSG,TEXT	"^PTUTIL V^"		/PROGRAM NAME AND VERSION.
	VERSION%12^66+VERSION+6060	/<HIGH VERSION DIGIT>/<LOW VERSION DIGIT>
	REVISION^100+"^-300		/REVISION
	TEXT	"  ^"


	PAGE

/	PRINT OUT FULL HEADER ROUTINE.

PRTITL,.-.				/PRINT FULL TITLE ROUTINE.
/	JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.
	JMP I	PRTITLE			/RETURN TO CALLER.

PGHEADE,.-.				/PRINT ENTIRE PAGE HEADER ROUTINE.
	DCA	PGFLAG			/SAVE PASSED HEADER PRINT VALUE.
	TAD	LINCNT			/GET CURRENT REMAINING LINES COUNTER.
	TAD	(-5)			/ADD ON HEADER OFFSET SO IT WILL
	DCA	LINCNT			/OUTPUT THE REST OF THE PAGE.
	JMS I	(PRCRLFS)		/PRINT OUT THE REST OF THE PREVIOUS PAGE.
	TAD	(-6)			/SETUP THE
	DCA	LINCNT			/TEAR-OFF COUNTER.
TEARLUP,TAD	("-&177)		/GET A MINUS SIGN.
	JMS I	[P7CH]			/PRINT IT.
	ISZ	LINCNT			/DONE ENOUGH?
	JMP	TEARLUP			/NO, GO BACK.
	JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.
	NL7775				/SETUP FOR
	DCA	LINCNT			/THREE <CR>/<LF>.
	JMS I	(PRCRLFS)		/GO PRINT THEM.
	ISZ	PGFLAG			/SHOULD WE PRINT THE HEADER?
	SKP				/SKIP IF SO.
	JMP I	PGHEADERPRINT		/NO, JUST RETURN.
	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/CALL MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE.
HSTZAP,	LSRMSG				/**** /F **** HSRMSG
	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/CALL MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE.
	TTLMSG				/TO PRINT MAIN TITLE MESSAGE.
	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/CALL MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE.
	DAYBLB				/TO PRINT DAY OF THE WEEK MESSAGE.
	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/CALL MESSAGE PRINT ROUTINE.
	DATMSG				/TO PRINT CURRENT DAY AND MONTH.
	JMS I	[DPRINT]		/PRINT OUT THE
	YRNUMLO				/CURRENT YEAR.
	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/PRINT OUT THE
	PAGMSG				/PAGE MESSAGE.
	ISZ	PGNUMLO			/BUMP THE LOW-ORDER PAGE NUMBER.
	SKP				/TYPICALLY DON'T BUMP THE HIGH-ORDER.
	ISZ	PGNUMHIGH		/BUMP THE HIGH-ORDER PAGE NUMBER.
	JMS I	[DPRINT]		/PRINT OUT THE
	PGNUMLO				/LATEST PAGE NUMBER.
	JMS I	[CRLF]			/FINISH HEADER WITH <CR>/<LF>.
	JMS I	[CRLF]			/DO AN EXTRA <CR>/<LF>.
	TAD	(-LINES)		/RESET THE
	DCA	LINCNT			/LINES COUNTER.
	JMP I	PGHEADERPRINT		/RETURN TO CALLER.
PGFLAG,	.-.				/ALSO PRINT NEW HEADER FLAG.
PGNUMLO,0				/LOW-ORDER PAGE NUMBER.
PGNUMHI,0				/HIGH-ORDER PAGE NUMBER.
YRNUMLO,ZBLOCK	2			/THE CURRENT YEAR IS STORED HERE [LOW-ORDER].

	PAGE				/DUMP LITERALS NOW.
/	PTUTIL INITIIALIZATION ROUTINES; MEMORY USED LATER FOR ALTERNATE PURPOSES.

/	COMES HERE FROM 00200.

PTINIT,	TAD I	(SWMX)			/GET PASSED OPTION SWITCHES /M-/X.
	AND	[10]			/JUST /U SWITCH BIT.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF /U OPTION SET.
	JMP	NOTU			/JUMP IF NOT.
	TAD	[CLA!400]		/GET GROUP 2 CLA INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(CASZP1)		/PREVENT UPPER-CASE THERE.
	TAD	[CLA!400]		/GET GROUP2 CLA INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(CASZP2)		/PREVENT UPPER-CASE THERE AS WELL.

/	DEBUGGING CHANGES THE LOGIC OF THE NEXT SECTION TO ALLOW DEVICE 66 OUTPUT.

	DEBNORM=SZA CLA			/NORMAL INSTRUCTION WHEN DEBUGGING IS DISABLED.

	DEBDEBU=SKP CLA			/INSTRUCTION USED WHEN DEBUGGING IS ENABLED.

	DEBOFFS=DEBDEBUSED-DEBNORM^DEBUG/DEBUGGING INSTRUCTION OFFSET.

NOTU,	NL0010				/SET AC TO 0010 IF PERHAPS DECMATE.
	NOP				/JUST IN CASE VERY STRANGE MACHINE.
	TAD	[-10]			/COMPARE TO MAGIC VALUE IF 6120 CPU.
	SZA CLA+DEBOFFSET		/SKIP IF A MATCH.
	JMP	CHKCOVRLAY		/JUMP IF NOT.

/	CERTAIN 6120-BASED SYSTEMS DO NOT USE THE INCOMPATIBLE 6121 SUPPORT CHIPS.  TO
/	PROPERLY SUPPORT THESE SYSTEMS, ALL P?S/8 PROGRAMS WILL INSTEAD CHECK FOR
/	INCOMPATIBLE CONSOLE IMPLEMENTATION [AND NOT MERELY CPU TYPE].

/	DEBUGGING CHANGES ALL CONSOLE OUTPUT INSTRUCTIONS TO THE DEVICE 66 EQUIVALENT.

	LPTCODE=66^10			/LINE PRINTER DEVICE CODE.

	OUTCODE=04^10			/CONSOLE OUTPUT DEVICE CODE.

	DEBUGOF=LPTCODE-OUTCODE^DEBUG	/OUTPUT INSTRUCTION OFFSET.

TSFCHEC,TSF+DEBUGOFFSET			/FLAG UP?
	SKP				/SKIP IF NOT.
	JMP	GOTFLAG			/JUMP IF SO.
	ISZ	TMOUT1			/WAITED LONG ENOUGH [INNER]?
	JMP	TSFCHECK		/NO, KEEP GOING.
	ISZ	TMOUT2			/WAITED LONG ENOUCH [OUTER]?
	JMP	TSFCHECK		/NO, KEEP GOING.

/	IF WE GET HERE, SOMETHING IS WRONG.  THE KEYBOARD MONITOR HANDS OFF CONTROL TO
/	ALL PROGRAMS WITH THE LAST CHARACTER PRINTING IN PROGRESS; THE FLAG SHOULD
/	HAVE RAISED BY NOW.

DMSET,	TLS+DEBUGOFFSET			/FORCE THE FLAG ON NOW.

/	COMES HERE IF CONSOLE IS INCOMPATIBLE OR SOME UNDEFINED CONDITION.

SETKRB,	ISZ I	(CHKKRS)		/BUMP "KRS" INSTRUCTION
	ISZ I	(CHKKRS)		/TO "KRB" INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(CHKKCC)		/DESTROY "KCC" INSTRUCTION.
	JMP	CHKCOVRLAY		/CONTINUE THERE.

/	COMES HERE IF THE CONSOLE OUTPUT FLAG CAME UP NORMALLY.

/	ON DECMATE SYSTEMS, THE 6121-BASED CONSOLE IMPLEMENTATION WILL CLEAR THE
/	OUTPUT FLAG; AS SUCH, TESTING THE FLAG AGAIN WILL FAIL TO SKIP.

GOTFLAG,TSF+DEBUGOFFSET			/TEST THE CONSOLE OUTPUT FLAG AGAIN.
	JMP	DMSET			/DECMATES WILL GET HERE.
/	JMP	CHKCOVRLAY		/RUNNING ON A COMPATIBLE SYSTEM, CONTINUE.
/	NOTE: THE CODE ABOVE GENERALLY FALLS THROUGH HERE.

CHKCOVR,NL0002				/SET CONSOLE OVERLAY ENABLED BIT MASK.
	AND I	(SCRSIZE)		/GET THE BIT.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF CONSOLE OVERLAY ENABLED.
	JMP	TSTFILES		/JUMP IF NOT.

/	THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS ENABLED; MAKE ALL THE PATCHES REQUIRED TO
/	SUPPORT THE OVERLAY CALLS.

/	LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY FIELD DETERMINATION.

/	THE LOGICAL CONSOLE IS CALLED BY A "CIF" INSTRUCTION TO ITS FIELD.  THE ACTUAL
/	FIELD VALUE IS CALCULATED USING THE MAXIMUM CORE SIZE [MCS] BITS, WHICH ARE
/	SET TO THE NEXT LOWER FIELD.  [NOTE: IN MOST CASES THIS IS THE PHYSICAL CORE
/	SIZE [PCS] VALUE; HOWEVER, THE CALCULATION USED HERE IS THE CORRECT WAY TO
/	DETERMINE THE PROPER FIELD.  THIS ALLOWS THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY TO OCCUPY
/	ADDITIONAL MEMORY FIELDS IF NECESSARY.]

	TAD I	(SCRSIZE)		/GET THE CORE SIZE WORD.
	RTR;RAR				/MOVE MCS BITS TO AC[6-8].
	AND	[70]			/JUST MCS BITS.
	TAD	(CIF	10)		/MAKE INTO "CIF MCS+10" INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(P7TSF)			/STORE OVER "TSF" INSTRUCTION.
/	ALL ADDITIONAL PATCHES TO SUPPORT THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY ARE DERIVED FROM
/	THE CURRENT INSTRUCTIONS IN MEMORY.

	TAD I	(P7JMP)			/GET "JMP P7AGAIN" INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(P7TLS)			/STORE OVER "TLS" INSTRUCTION.
	TAD	(JMS	OUTCON)		/GET OUTPUT CALL INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(P7JMP)			/STORE OVER "JMP P7AGAIN" INSTRUCTION.
	TAD I	(P7TSF)			/GET "CIF MCS+10" INSTRUCTION AGAIN.
	DCA I	(P7OCHK)		/STORE OVER "TSF" INSTRUCTION.
	TAD I	(P7OJMP)		/GET "JMP P7OCHK" INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(P7OTLS)		/STORE OVER "TLS" INSTRUCTION.
	TAD	(JMS	OUTCON)		/GET OUTPUT CALL INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(P7OJMP)		/STORE OVER "JMP P7OCHK" INSTRUCTION.
	TAD I	(P7TSF)			/GET "CIF MCS+10" INSTRUCTION AGAIN.
	DCA I	(CHKKSF)		/STORE OVER "KSF" INSTRUCTION,
	TAD I	(CHKJMP)		/GET "JMP I CTLCTST" INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(CHKKRS)		/STORE OVER "KRS" [OR "KRB"] INSTRUCTION.
	TAD	(JMS	INCON)		/GET INPUT CALL INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(CHKJMP)		/STORE OVER "JMP I CTLCTST" INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	(CHKKCC)		/DESTROY "KCC" INSTRUCTION.

/	CHECK FOR A LIST OF PASSED FILES.

TSTFILE,TAD I	[SFILES]		/GET FIRST FILE ARGUMENT.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF NO FILES.
	JMP	TSTMIXED		/JUMP IF SOME FILES.
	JMS I	(SCRIBE)		/COMPLAIN OF
	NOFLMSG				/NO FILES PASSED.
	JMP I	[SBOOT]			/GOODBYE!

/	CHECK IF FILES ARE EITHER ALL OUTPUT OR ALL INPUT; MIXED FILES NOT ALLOWED.

TSTMIXE,TAD I	(SOUTFLS)		/GET OUTPUT FILE COUNT, ETC. WORD.
	AND	[37]			/JUST FILE COUNT BITS.
	DCA	OUTCNT			/STORE IT FOR NOW.

/	IF THE OUTPUT FILE COUNT IS ZERO, THERE IS NO POSSIBILITY OF MIXED FILES.

	TAD	OUTCNT			/GET THE OUTPUT FILE COUNT BACK.
	SNA				/SKIP IF SOME OUTPUT FILES.
	JMP	NOTMIXED		/JUMP IF THERE AREN'T ANY.

/	IF THE LIST IS FULL LENGTH, ALL THE FILES ARE OUTPUT FILES.

	TAD	[SFILES]		/POINT PAST THE LIST OF OUTPUT FILES.
	SNA				/SKIP IF NOT MAXIMUM LIST SIZE.
	JMP	NOTMIXED		/MAXIMUM AMOUNT OF FILES PASSED, ALL OUTPUT.
/	CHECK TO SEE IF THE LIST DELIMITER IS JUST PAST THE LAST OUTPUT FILE.

	DCA	WRKPT0			/STASH POINTER TO LIST POSITION PAST OUTPUT.
	TAD I	WRKPT0			/GET THE LIST ELEMENT VALUE.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF INPUT FILE PASSED AFTER OUTPUT FILES.
	JMP	NOTMIXED		/JUMP IF ONLY OUTPUT FILES.
	JMS I	 (SCRIBE)		/COMPLAIN OF
	MXFLMSG				/MIXED FILES PASSED.
	JMP I	[SBOOT]			/GOODBYE!

/	IF WE GET HERE THE LIST OF FILES IS PURELY INPUT FILES OR PURELY OUTPUT FILES.

	NOTMIXE=.			/FILE LIST IS NOT MIXED IF WE GET HERE.

	JMP I	(UNITEST)		/CONTINE ON NEXT PAGE.

TMOUT1,	0				/INNER TIME-OUT COUNTER.
TMOUT2,	-144				/OUTER TIME-OUT COUNTER.
WRKPT0,	.-.				/FILE CHECKING POINTER.

	PAGE				/DUMP LITERALS NOW.
/	CHECK TO SEE IF ALL PASSED FILE HANDLES ARE UNIQUE; EACH HANDLE WILL BE
/	COMPARED TO ALL OTHERS IN THE FILE LIST.

UNITEST,ISZ	WRKPT1			/BUMP TO NEXT FILE HANDLE TO BE TESTED.
	TAD I	WRKPT1			/GET THE LATEST FILE HANDLE [NOTE: COULD SKIP!]
	SNA				/SKIP IF MORE TO TEST.
	JMP	ALLUNIQUE		/ALL ARE UNIQUE; WE'RE DONE.
	CIA				/INVERT NOW TO SPEED LATER TESTING.
	DCA	TESTHANDLE		/STORE IT FOR COMPARISON LATER.
	TAD	WRKPT1			/GET THE LATEST FILE HANDLE ADDRESS.
	CIA				/INVERT NOW TO SPEED LATER TESTING.
	DCA	TESTHPTR		/WILL BE USED TO AVOID SELF-TESTING.

/	CHECK TO SEE IF LATEST FILE HANDLE VALUE APPEARS ELSEWHERE IN THE LIST.

	TAD	(SFILES-1)		/SETUP THE
	DCA	WRKPT2			/SEARCH POINTER.
SRCHLP,	ISZ	WRKPT2			/BUMP TO NEXT FILE HANDLE TO TEST.
	TAD I	WRKPT2			/GET THE FILE HANDLE VALUE [NOTE: COULD SKIP!]
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF NOT AT END OF THE FILE LIST.
	JMP	UNITEST			/THIS ONE PASSED; GO CHECK THE REST.

/	MAKE SURE WE DON'T COMPARE LATEST ELEMENT TO ITSELF.

	TAD	WRKPT2			/GET LATEST FILE HANDLE POINTER ADDRESS.
	TAD	TESTHPTR		/COMPARE TO TEST FILE HANDLE ADDRESS.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF DIFFERENT
	JMP	SRCHLP			/JUMP TO AVOID SELF-TESTING.
	TAD I	WRKPT2			/GET LATEST FILE HANDLE VALUE.
	TAD	TESTHANDLE		/COMPARE TO TEST FILE HANDLE.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF A MATCH.
	JMP	SRCHLP			/GO BACK IF DIFFERENT.

/	ONE OF THE FILE HANDLES MATCHES THE LATEST TEST FILE HANDLE.  COMPLAIN ABOUT
/	DUPLICATE FILE USAGE.

	JMS I	(SCRIBE)		/CALL MESSAGE PRINTER
	ONOMSG				/PRINT "ONE OR MORE" MESSAGE.
	TAD	OUTCNT			/GET OUTPUT FILE COUNT.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF ALL INPUT FILES.
	TAD	(OUTMSG-INMSG)		/ADD MESSAGE OFFSET.
	TAD	IOMSG			/GET INPUT MESSAGE ADDRESS.
	DCA	IOMSG			/STASH IN-LINE POINTER
	JMS I	(SCRIBE)		/CALL MESSAGE PRINTER.
IOMSG,	INMSG+.-.			/PRINT INPUT [OR OUTPUT] MESSAGE.
	JMS I	 (SCRIBE)		/COMPLAIN OF
	DUFLMSG				/DUPLICATE FILE USAGE.
	JMP I	[SBOOT]			/GOODBYE!
/	IF WE GET HERE THE LIST OF FILES IS PURELY INPUT FILES OR PURELY OUTPUT FILES
/	AND ALL ARE UNIQUE.

	ALLUNIQ=.			/ALL PASSED FILES ARE UNIQUE IF WE GET HERE.

/	UNTIL P?S/8 VERSION 9A IS RELEASED, WE CANNOT PROCESS THE FILE HANDLES ANY
/	FURTHER.  FUTURE RELEASES WILL ENSURE ALL OUTPUT FILES ARE EITHER TFS FILES OR
/	EXTENDED-LENGTH FILES AS REQUIRED [DEPENDING ON WHETHER OR NOT THE /E OPTION
/	SWITCH WAS SET].  FOR THE PRESENT, THE USER MUST BE AWARE OF THE RESTRICTIONS
/	OF THE PREVAILING WORKAROUND [USE A PROPERLY POSITIONED TFS FILE IN LIEU OF
/	THE EXTENDED-LENGTH FILE.

/	NOTE: WHEN EXTENDED-LENGTH FILES ARE PROPERLY SUPPORTED, THE LIMIT VALUE OF
/	THE TFS DIRECTORY SHOULD BE TESTED AGAINST THE STARTING BLOCK FOR EACH
/	EXTENDED-LENGTH FILE DIRECTORY ENTRY [LOCATED IN THE SYSTEM PROGRAMS DIRECTORY
/	AS A SPECIAL STUB ENTRY FOR THE SINGLE EXTENDED FILE ALLOWED ON EACH LOGICAL
/	UNIT].

/	INPUT FILES DO NOT REQUIRE FURTHER TESTING BECAUSE THERE IS NO ISSUE WHEN
/	CREATING PAPER-TAPE OUTPUT.

	ZBLOCK	100			/RESERVED FOR FUTURE FILE TESTS.

	JMP I	(TESTMORE)		/CONTINUE THERE.

TESTHAN,.-.				/LATEST TEST FILE HANDLE.
TESTHPT,.-.				/LATEST TEST FILE HANDLE ADDRESS.
WRKPT1,	SFILES-1			/FILE UNIQUENESS POINTER; INITIALIZED FOR TEST.
WRKPT2,	.-.				/FILE CHECKING POINTER.

	PAGE				/DUMP LITERALS NOW.
/	INITIALIZATION CONTINUES HERE.

TESTMOR,TAD I	(SWY9)			/GET THE /Y THROUGH /9 OPTION SWITCHES.
	AND	(200)			/JUST THE /2 BIT.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF CLEAR.
	DCA I	(HIZAP)			/PREVENT UNBUFFERED ROUTINE IF SET.
	TAD I	(SWAL)			/GET THE /A THROUGH /L OPTION SWITCHES.
	AND	(100)			/JUST /F SWITCH.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF /F SWITCH SET.
	JMP	NOTF			/JUMP IF NOT
	TAD	(HSRMSG)		/GET HIGH-SPEED READER MESSAGE ADDRESS.
	DCA I	(HSTZAP)		/STORE IN-LINE.

/	PERFORM OTHER /F-RELATED STUFF HERE.

	JMP	PASTF			/GO PAST NON-/F STUFF.

/	COMES HERE TO PERFORM STUFF IF /F IS NOT SET.

NOTF,

/	COMES HERE TO AVOID NON-/F STUFF.	

PASTF,	JMS I	(GETDATE)		/SETUP THE DATE-RELATED STUFF.
	JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.
	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/CALL MESSAGE PRINTER ROUTINE TO
	PROGMSG				/PRINT PROGRAM OPENING MESSAGE.
	JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.
	TAD I	(SOUTFLS)		/GET OUTPUT FILE COUNT.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF OUTPUTTING FILES.
	JMP	PUNCHING		/JUMP IF PUNCHING TAPE FROM INPUT FILES.

/	COMES HERE IF OUTPUT FILES WILL BE CREATED; DETERMINE WHICH TYPE.

	TAD I	(SWAL)			/GET THE PASSED OPTION SWITCHES /A-/L.
	AND	[200]			/JUST THE /E SWITCH.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF SET.
	JMP	TFSOUT			/JUMP IF CLEAR.

/	EXTENDED-LENGTH OUTPUT FILES WILL BE CREATED.

	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/CALL MESSAGE PRINTER ROUTINE TO
	ELOMSG				/INDICATE EXTENDED-LENGTH FILES.

/	DO OTHER EXTENDED-LENGTH FILE INITIALIZATION HERE.

	JMP	OUTCOMMON		/CONTINUE THERE.
/	COMES HERE IF TFS OUTPUT FILES WILL BE CREATED.

TFSOUT,	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/CALL MESSAGE PRINTER ROUTINE TO
	TFSOMSG				/INDICATE TFS OUTPUT FILES.

/	DO OTHER TFS OUTPUT FILE STUFF HERE.

/	JMP	OUTCOMMON		/CONTINUE THERE

OUTCOMM,JMP I	(OUTFILES)		/CONTINUE THERE TO PROCESS OUTPUT FILES.

	JMS I	[DPRINT]		/PRINT
	DPFOO				/TEST VALUE.
	JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.
	JMS I	(INTAPE)		/GET ENTIRE PAPER-TAPE INPUT STREAM
	JMS I	(PRTITLE)		/PRINT A TITLE PAGE.
	JMS I	[CRLF]			/PRINT <CR>/<LF>.
	JMS I	[SCRIBE]		/PRINT THE
	FOOMSG				/HELLO WORLD MESSAGE FOR LAUGHS.
	JMP I	[SBOOT]			/FOR NOW.

/	EVENTUALLY GO TO THE SECTION THAT PROCESSES INPUT TAPES TO OUTPUT FILES.

PUNCHIN,JMP I	[SBOOT]			/FOR NOW UNTIL WE WRITE THIS PART!

/	TEMPORARY STUFF; GET RID OF THIS SOON!

DPFOO,	7777;	7777			/A LARGE VALUE TO PRINT.
FOOMSG,	TEXT	"%^H^ELLO ^W^ORLD!%%"	/TEMPORARY MESSAGE.

	PAGE				/DUMP LITERALS NOW.
/	GET TODAY'S DATE AND RELATED INFORMATION ROUTINE.

/	NOTE: THE CODE USED HERE WILL FAIL IN THE YEAR 2100; HOWEVER, SINCE THE P?S/8
/	DATE FORMAT IS BEING OVERHAULED IN VERSION 9A, WE WILL COPY THE ALGORITHM USED
/	IN ALL OTHER P?S/8 PROGRAMS PRESENTLY.  WHEN THE FULL DATE IS STORED IN
/	MEMORY, THE PROPER CALCULATION OF INTERCALARY YEARS WILL BE USED.

/	THE PRESENT DATE IS BASED ON 01-JAN-1960 FOR AN IMPLIED BASE YEAR GROUP OF
/	0.  ADD ONE TO THE BASE YEAR GROUP FOR EACH ADDITIONAL EIGHT YEARS.  SINCE THE
/	ALGORITHM SUPPORTS AT LEAST 11 YEAR INTERVALS, THE BASE YEAR GROUP IN EFFECT
/	HAS TO BE PATCHED EXTREMELY INFREQUENTLY, [BUT MORE OFTEN THAN NEVER].  AS OF
/	P?S/8 VERSION 8Z, A CHANGE LOG WILL RECORD ALL SPECIFIC STORAGE BLOCK WORDS
/	THAT MUST BE UPDATED AT THE SAME TIME; PTUTIL'S ENTRY WILL BE ADDED ONCE THE
/	PROGRAM IS RELEASED.  [NOTE: IT IS STRONGLY RECOMMENDED ALL BSGRP REFERENCES
/	BE UPGRADED IN 2016; FAILING TO DO SO MEANS THE DATE WILL RUN OUT IN 2019.
/	THUS, AS OF THIS EDIT, THERE IS PLENTY OF TIME.]

	DECIMAL				/MAKE CALCULATIONS A BIT EASIER.

GETDATE,.-.				/GET THE DATE INFO ROUTINE.
	CLA				/CLEAN UP.
	TAD	(28)			/RESET THE
	DCA I	(FEBENT)		/FEBRUARY LENGTH.
	TAD	(JANENT)		/POINT TO THE FIRST
	DCA	ENTPTR			/MONTH OF THE YEAR.
	TAD I	(SDATE)			/GET THE SYSTEM DATE WORD.
	JMS	DIVIDE;	372		/372 DAYS IN 12 MONTHS OF 31 DAYS EACH.
	DCA	YEAR			/SAVE RELATIVE YEAR IN THIS BASE YEAR GROUP.
	TAD	REM			/GET DAYS LEFT IN THE YEAR.
	JMS	DIVIDE;	31		/DIVIDE BY 31.
	DCA	MONTH			/SAVE RELATIVE MONTH.
	TAD	REM			/GET RELATIVE DAY OF THE MONTH.
	IAC				/NEED ORIGIN ONE VALUE.
	DCA	DAY			/SAVE OUR DAY.
	TAD	YEAR			/GET THE YEAR.
	TAD	(3)			/ROUND UP FOR LEAP YEARS.
	CLL RAR;CLL RAR			/DIVIDE BY FOUR.
	DCA	LPYRCT			/SAVE AS EXTRA LEAP DAYS COUNT.
	TAD	YEAR			/GET THE YEAR AGAIN.
	AND	(3)			/JUST LEAP BITS.
	SNA CLA				/SKIP IF NOT A LEAP YEAR.
	ISZ I	(FEBENT)		/BUMP FEBRUARY ENTRY TO 29 IN A LEAP YEAR.
	TAD	MONTH			/GET THE MONTH.
	CMA				/INVERT FOR COUNTING.
	DCA	MONCNT			/STASH IT.
	JMP	MONBMP			/GO CHECK THERE FIRST.

MONADD,	TAD I	ENTPTR			/GET A PREVIOUS MONTH'S DAY COUNT VALUE.
	ISZ	ENTPTR			/BUMP TO NEXT MONTH FOR NEXT TIME.
MONBMP,	ISZ	MONCNT			/DONE ENOUGH PRIOR MONTHS?
	JMP	MONADD			/NO, KEEP GOING.
	TAD	DAY			/ADD ON DAY.
	TAD	YEAR			/ADD ON YEAR.
	TAD	LPYRCT			/ADD ON EXTRA LEAP DAYS.
	TAD	BSGROUP			/\
	TAD	BSGROUP			/ >ADD ON BASE INFLUENCE.
	TAD	BSGROUP			//
	JMS	DIVIDE;	7		/SEVEN DAYS IN A WEEK [NOT EIGHT].
	CLA				/THROW AWAY WEEK COUNTER.
	TAD	REM			/GET THE REMAINDER.
	CLL RAL				/MULTIPLY BY TWO.
	TAD	REM			/MULTIPLY BY THREE.
	RAL				/MULTIPLY BY SIX.
	TAD	(DAYS-1)		/POINT TO PROPER DAY STRING [-1 FOR AUTO-INDEX].
	DCA	XR1			/STASH THE AUTO-INDEX GET POINTER.
	TAD	(DAYBLB-1)		/SETUP THE
	DCA	XR2			/AUTO-INDEX STORE POINTER.
	TAD	(DAYS-DAYS2)		/SETUP THE
	DCA	XR0			/MOVE COUNT.
MVDAYLP,TAD I	XR1			/GET A WORD.
	DCA I	XR2			/PUT A WORD.
	ISZ	XR0			/DONE YET?
	JMP	MVDAYLP			/NO, GO BACK.
	TAD	(MONTXT-1)		/SETUP THE
	DCA	XR1			/AUTO-INDEX STORE POINTER.
	TAD	MONTH			/GET THE MONTH.
	CLL RAL				/*2
	TAD	MONTH			/*3 FOR TRIPLE WORD MOVES.
	TAD	(MONLST-1)		/ADD ON LIST POINTER.
	DCA	XR2			/STASH THE STRING POINTER.
	TAD I	XR2			/GET FIRST PAIR.
	DCA I	XR1			/STORE IN MESSAGE.
	TAD I	XR2			/GET SECOND PAIR.
	DCA I	XR1			/STORE IN MESSAGE.
	TAD I	XR2			/GET THIRD PAIR.
	DCA I	XR1			/STORE IN MESSAGE.
	TAD	BSGROUP			/GET THE BASE YEAR GROUP
	CLL RTL;RAL			/*8
	TAD	YEAR			/ADD ON RELATIVE YEAR.
	TAD	(1960)			/ADD ON ORIGIN YEAR.
	DCA I	(YRNUMLOW)		/STORE FOR PRINTING LATER.
	TAD	DAY			/GET DAY OF THE MONTH.
	JMS	DIVIDE;	10		/GET TENS DIGIT.
	CLL RTL;RTL;RTL			/MOVE TO HIGH-ORDER
	TAD	REM			/ADD ON UNITS DIGIT.
	TAD	("0^64+"0-128)		/MAKE THEM ASCII SIX-BIT.
	DCA I	(DAYNUM)		/STORE IN THE MESSAGE TEXT.
	JMP I	GETDATE			/RETURN TO CALLER.

/	NOTE: THE DATE CODING DOESN'T TAKE INTO ACCOUNT THE 400 YEAR EXCEPTION TO THE
/	100 YEAR EXCEPTION TO THE LEAP YEAR EVERY FOURTH YEAR RULE.
	OCTAL				/BACK TO NORMAL.

/	DIVIDE ROUTINE.

DIVIDE,	.-.				/DIVIDE ROUTINE.
	DCA	REM			/SAVE IN REMAINDER.
	DCA	QUO			/CLEAR QUOTIENT.
	TAD	REM			/GET IT BACK.
	STL CIA				/INVERT.
	SKP				/DON'T FIRST TIME.
DVLOOP,	ISZ	QUO			/BUMP UP QUOTIENT.
	TAD I	DIVIDE			/ADD ON ARGUMENT.
	SNA SZL				/UNDERFLOW?
	JMP	DVLOOP			/NO, KEEP GOING.
	CIA				/YES, INVERT IT BACK.
	TAD I	DIVIDE			/RESTORE LOST VALUE.
	DCA	REM			/SAVE AS REMAINDER.
	TAD	QUO			/GET THE QUOTIENT.
	ISZ	DIVIDE			/BUMP PAST ARGUMENT.
	JMP I	DIVIDE			/RETURN.

BSGROUP,BSGRP				/CURRENT BASE YEAR GROUP VALUE.
DAY,	.-.				/RELATIVE DAY.
ENTPTR,	.-.				/MONTH LENGTH TABLE POINTER.
LPYRCT,	.-.				/LEAP YEAR DAYS COUNT.
MONCNT,	.-.				/MONTH COUNTER.
MONTH,	.-.				/RELATIVE MONTH.
QUO,	.-.				/DIVIDE QUOTIENT.
REM,	.-.				/DIVIDE REMAINDER.
YEAR,	.-.				/RELATIVE YEAR.

	PAGE				/DUMP LITERALS NOW.
/	MONTH LENGTH TABLE.

	DECIMAL				/MAKE IT EASIER.

JANENT,	31				/31 DAYS IN JANUARY.
FEBENT,	28				/29 IN LEAP YEAR!
	31				/31 DAYS IN MARCH.
	30				/30 DAYS IN APRIL.
	31				/31 DAYS IN MAY.
	30				/30 DAYS IN JUNE.
	31				/31 DAYS IN JULY.
	31				/31 DAYS IN AUGUST.
	30				/30 DAYS IN SEPTEMBER.
	31				/31 DAYS IN OCTOBER.
	30				/30 DAYS IN NOVEMBER.
/	31				/31 DAYS IN DECEMBER.

	OCTAL				/BACK TO NORMAL.
/	DAYS OF THE WEEK STRINGS.

/	NOTE: ALL STRINGS IN THE TABLE OCCUPY SIX WORDS FOR ALIGNMENT PURPOSES; IN
/	THIS PROGRAM, THEY MUST TERMINATE THE ENTIRE STRING FOR PRINTING PURPOSES
/	[WITH A TRAILING HALF-WORD OF 00].  IF THE SPECIFIC REQUIREMENTSS ARE ALTERED,
/	IT IS POSSIBLE FOR THE WEDNESDAY ENTRY [AT THE END OF THE TABLE] TO BECOME ONE
/	WORD LONGER THAN THE OTHER ENTRIES.  ASSUMING THE ALLOCATED SPACE IN THE
/	MESSAGE IS CORRECTLY FORMULATED, IT IS QUITE ACCEPTABLE THIS ENTRY BECOMES ONE
/	WORD LONGER THAN THE OTHERS.

DAYS,	TEXT	"^T^HURSDAY^"		/THURSDAY.
DAYS2,	TEXT	"^F^RIDAY^^^"		/FRIDAY.
	TEXT	"^S^ATURDAY^"		/SATURDAY.
	TEXT	"^S^UNDAY^^^"		/SUNDAY.
	TEXT	"^M^ONDAY^^^"		/MONDAY.
	TEXT	"^T^UESDAY^^"		/TUESDAY.
	TEXT	"^W^EDNESDAY"		/WEDNESDAY.
/	MONTH STRINGS.

MONLST,	TEXT	"-J^AN-"		/JANUARY.
	TEXT	"-F^EB-"		/FEBRUARY.
	TEXT	"-M^AR-"		/MARCH.
	TEXT	"-A^PR-"		/APRIL.
	TEXT	"-M^AY-"		/MAY.
	TEXT	"-J^UN-"		/JUNE.
	TEXT	"-J^UL-"		/JULY.
	TEXT	"-A^UG-"		/AUGUST.
	TEXT	"-S^EP-"		/SEPTEMBER.
	TEXT	"-O^CT-"		/OCTOBER.
	TEXT	"-N^OV-"		/NOVEMBER.
	TEXT	"-D^EC-"		/DECEMBER.
/	ONCE-ONLY ERROR MESSAGE STRINGS.

