but too many copies around [just enough] so we have to come up with something.

Perhaps add some new sub-system ["Build Number"] that designates it's still Version
8Z, but the original 8Z is no build versus a build higher.  The best way would be
to appropriate some other page zero location currently 0000 anyway, but release a
patch with the build added [and upgrade SYSTAT to be aware of it].

Version 8Z [with the 0000]

and then Version 8Z [with non-zero].  Just define Build Number= something like
value of the word on page zero + 100 decimal or even have decimal points:

Thus, old 8Z systems, SYSTAT reports 8Z  but newer SYSTAT would report
old 8Z as Build [revision?  Talk about that with Bob] 1.00.  That way, the
newer patched and revised slightly 8Z becomes say Build/Revision 2.01 or
